commit 8aeda3d4b6
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 18:27:23 2026 +1000

    WiMAX: Don't register the generic CRC expert info name twice

    The 4.4 backport of "WiMAX: Fix UCD loop, CID limit and several
    decoding errors" registered the new "CRC missing - the frame is too
    short" expert info as wmx.genericCrc.missing, the name of the existing
    "CRC is not included" note. The second registration replaced the first
    in the name lookup, so filtering on wmx.genericCrc.missing no longer
    found the note. Use wmx.genericCrc.missing_mal as master, 5.0 and 4.6
    do.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

commit d580c7ab70
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 14:14:19 2026 +1000

    PROFINET: Fix recursion and several bounds problems in PN-RT/SXP/MRP/DCP

    PN-RT: a reassembled FRAG PDU is handed back to the ethertype table and
    can be PN-RT again; its inner FRAG PDU shares the reassembly ID of the
    same frame, so the same data was dissected again until the layer limit
    was hit. Do not reassemble again while dissecting a reassembled PN-RT
    frame (nesting counter via p_get_proto_depth()). The reassembly key
    shifted the frame number by 2 but the fragment ID has 4 bits, so keys
    of different frames collided; shift by 4. The per-ID start table is now
    only updated on the first pass and the key is kept per frame with
    p_add_proto_data().

    SXP: the per-conversation service type cache was updated on every pass,
    so the Info column of a middle fragment differed between one pass and
    two passes. Update the cache only on the first pass and store the
    resolved service type per PDU for later passes.

    PROFINET: pn_find_aruuid_frame_setup() returned the last list entry
    when nothing matched; return NULL (all callers check for NULL).

    RSI: the unsigned test "length - offset - ... > 0" was always true;
    use signed remaining length. Register the reassembly table in
    proto_register instead of an init routine (RSI and SXP).

    MRP: test the remaining length of the tvb that offset belongs to,
    dissect unknown TLVs from that tvb, add the LinkInfo bitmask to the
    TLV tree, and do not wrap the uint8 length on short TLVs.

    PTCP: an unknown TLV advanced the offset twice and was added to the
    wrong tree.

    DCP: stop the option loop for odd block lengths, reject a too short
    Configuration Domain block, and check the PDU is at least 10 bytes
    before reading the length in the heuristic.

    4.4: Hand-ported. This branch has no SXP dissector, no RSI security
    dissector and no MRP InLink dissector, so those hunks are dropped.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit bba73eced3954556392deb35a3dd179f970efcd9)

commit fd6d45fcfa
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 14:12:01 2026 +1000

    PROFINET: Fix crashes, CPU blow-ups and per-pass state in PN-IO

    The Read/Write request and response header blocks, and the RTC1 object
    extraction, compared the stored device and controller MAC addresses
    with memcmp() over six bytes of pinfo->dl_src/dl_dst without checking
    the address type. On a link without Ethernet addresses (for example raw
    IP carrying UDP port 34962) the data pointer is NULL and the second
    packet crashed. The addresses are now only stored and used when both
    are Ethernet addresses, and compared with addresses_equal().

    The PROFIenergy float64 measurement values (Set_Meter and
    Query_Measurement) were dissected with dissect_dcerpc_uint64() into an
    FT_DOUBLE field, which is a dissector bug report (an abort with
    WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG) and reads an uninitialized flag. They
    are now added with proto_tree_add_item().

    With a GSD path configured, resolve_pa_profile_submodule_name() wrote up
    to MAX_NAMELENGTH bytes into a module name pointer that had been
    redirected to the exact-size GSD text, a heap overflow that also
    corrupted the GSD cache. The GSD text is now copied into the
    MAX_NAMELENGTH buffer.

    dissect_block() ignored the offset returned by the block body
    dissectors and advanced by the declared body length, but several
    dissectors (PDevData, IandM5, AssetManagementInfo, the CIM blocks) read
    past their declared body, so the enclosing loop dissected the same bytes
    again. A chain of N nested blocks cost 2^N or Fibonacci(N) block
    dissections. Every block body dissector now gets a tvb subset that ends
    at the declared body end (offsets stay absolute), so nesting is linear.
    The IandM5 and AssetManagementInfo entry loops also stop at the end of
    their data.

    IOCRBlockReq searched the station's IO data object and IOCS lists
    linearly for every entry (and allocated an object even for duplicates),
    quadratic in the number of entries. The lists now have a hash index by
    slot/subslot, and an object is only allocated when it is new.

    The AR list was a GList searched and appended to linearly, quadratic in
    the number of ARs. It is now a wmem_map keyed by the ARUUID.

    dissect_PNIO_C_SDU_RTC1() walked the whole object list for every object
    of every RTC1 frame. It now finds the object by frame offset in a hash
    index that is extended lazily with the entries added to the list. Each
    object count iteration looks up one IO data object and one IOCS object
    instead of scanning the lists, which gives the same result for
    well-formed configurations.

    The AR records were modified on every pass, and the "changed from"
    expert infos and the ARUUID/MAC information shown for a frame read the
    state left by all frames, so -2 and the GUI showed different PN-IO data
    than the first pass. The records are now only updated while the frame
    has not been visited. pnio_ar_info() keeps a per-frame copy of the AR
    state from the first pass and shows it on later passes, the "changed
    from" warnings are remembered per frame and shown again, and an AR is
    not found by frames before the one that created it. The conversation
    filter data now refers to the per-frame copy and is set instead of
    being prepended to file scope data on every pass.

    The RTC1 dissector no longer rewrites the PROFIsafe toggle bit and
    status byte state, and no longer allocates a new module name string for
    every object of every frame, after the first pass.

    hf_pn_io_gating_cycle (PDSyncData v1.0/v1.2 and the CIMNetConf blocks)
    was never registered, so those blocks ended in an "Unregistered hf"
    dissector bug report (an abort with WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG).
    Register it. Also do not call g_dir_close() on a GSD directory that
    could not be opened.

    Small fixes: reduce the RS_TimeStatus extension length by the optional
    time stamp so it is not decoded twice, guard the vendor specific fiber
    optic data length against underflow, fix the TxPortGroup array size
    precedence, and use int for two offsets that were 16 bit.

    4.4: Hand-ported, on top of the partial backport 0abfe269f0 that already
    gave the block body dissectors a tvb subset and bounded the IandM5 and
    AssetManagementInfo loops; this adds the rest. This branch has no
    conversation_address_list, GSD cache, ARSXP or CIM blocks, so the MAC
    address, GSD cache and those block hunks are dropped. The module name
    overflow is fixed where the Expected Submodule data is copied into the
    IO data object, and the unregistered hf_pn_io_gating_cycle does not
    exist here.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 5c3a303860394fb649b940de9b13d37725453f95)

commit 6b640bc115
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    WiMAX: Make map decoding independent of earlier frames and fix a loop

    A compressed DL-MAP or Reduced AAS DL-MAP inside a PDU burst was always
    decoded from the start of the burst, not from the current offset, and
    the IE loop was bounded by the burst length, not by the map length. A
    burst made of many 4-byte map headers decoded the whole map again for
    every header, which is quadratic in the burst size and ran into the
    tree item limits. Decode from a subset at the current offset and stop
    the IE loop at the CRC, with an expert info if IEs are left over. The
    unsigned "length -= 15" that wrapped for short maps is clamped.

    Whether a frame is downlink was decided from bs_address, which is set
    by the first FCH burst in the file, so the decision for a frame
    dissected before it changed on the second pass. Decide it once per
    frame and keep it with p_add_proto_data().

    The compact DL-/UL-MAP state (harq_mode, cid_type, max_logical_bands,
    band AMC type and symbol counts) and N_layer and RCID_Type were never
    reset, so a map was decoded with the state left by earlier frames and,
    with a second pass, by later ones. Reset them at the start of each
    HARQ-MAP, DL-MAP, compressed DL-MAP, Reduced AAS DL-MAP and UL-MAP.
    cqich_id_size is deliberately left alone, it carries the UCD setting.

    Generate the CRC tables once at registration instead of on each PDU
    burst, so that a HARQ-MAP or MAC header reached without a burst is not
    checked against an empty table. The plugin.c generator does not match
    the handoff functions of the AAS feedback, ARQ, DREG and PMC messages
    to a protocol, so they were never called; call them from
    proto_reg_handoff_wimax().

    Fix small errors: the TLV length check in the m2m dissector compared
    the TLV start and reported every TLV as malformed; the HARQ_DL_MAP_IE
    length is 8 bits, not 2; the IR CTC/CC Dedicated_DL_Control_IE and
    RCID_IE results were added to the bit offset in the wrong unit; the
    appended UL-MAP of a Reduced AAS DL-MAP was decoded from bit 0; the
    invalid nested TLV items in the CS parameter decoder used a negative
    length; the Short-HMAC digest length subtracted an absolute offset; the
    DL-MAP CRC-16 field was FT_UINT32, so the checksum read 4 bytes and the
    end of every Reduced AAS DL-MAP was malformed.

    4.4: wimax_compact_dlmap_ie_decoder.h has no extern declarations of
    the state variables on this branch, so only the declaration of
    wimax_reset_compact_map_state() is added.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit df1131d982ac06d0cc19dad6715a459aaa9897b5)

commit d9bf3ed5e4
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    opcua: Fix nesting state leaks and per-pass encryption state

    The nesting counters (the per-frame Variant/DataValue counter and
    pinfo->dissection_depth) were not restored when an exception ended a
    message. tcp_dissect_pdus() goes on with the next UA message in the
    frame, so the leaked levels added up over the messages of one segment
    until increment_dissection_depth() hit its DISSECTOR_ASSERT. Run each
    message from a wrapper that resets the counter and restores both
    values, also on an exception.

    The encryption mode kept in the conversation was rewritten on every
    pass, so a frame before the OpenSecureChannel was dissected with the
    state left behind by the last message, and "tshark -2" differed from
    one pass. Only change the conversation on the first pass, and keep the
    mode and signature length each message started with in per-frame
    protocol data, keyed by the message number within the frame.

    Also: skip the 4 byte ArrayDimensions length of an oversized Variant
    instead of returning with the counter raised and the offset unchanged;
    give the X.509 decoder a tvb limited to the certificate ByteString;
    stop the signature (Sign) and padding plus signature (SignAndEncrypt)
    lengths from wrapping when the message is shorter, with a new expert
    info; print the NUL-terminated copy of a keylog DSB in the debug
    message, not the raw block; log "no keyset found" only when there is
    none.

    4.4: This branch has no AEAD decryption and no ws_debug; the
    footer length guard is also added in decrypt_opcua() before the
    padding byte is read, and the keylog DSB copy uses g_malloc0 instead
    of reading one byte past the block.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit fc0c9c07c9529bced1eafd10bb2ad16da2145d17)

commit 012a97ff1d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    usbdump: Bound the packet length and fix state and error handling

    The captured length from the frame header went to the buffer
    allocation unchecked, so a small (compressed) file could make the
    reader allocate up to 4 GiB. Reject lengths larger than
    WTAP_MAX_PACKET_SIZE_USBPCAP (128 MiB), the limit for USB
    encapsulations.

    Also print the converted version in the unsupported-version message and
    return WTAP_OPEN_ERROR, since an error is set. Do not let a random
    access read change the sequential multiframe tracking, and stop ignoring
    a failed read of the next multiframe size.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit e7e95ec8aada056910023fb8bb5a1366f8d8ba6a)

commit efe75c9aba
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    WiMAX: Fix UCD loop, CID limit and several decoding errors

    The UCD Uplink Burst Profile sub-TLV loop did not check the sub-TLV
    length. A 4-byte length of 0xFFFFFFFA wrapped length + value offset to
    zero and the loop never advanced, hanging tshark. Stop on a length
    above MAX_TLV_LEN or below 1, as the DCD and REG loops do.

    The generic MAC header decoder reported a dissector bug when a 65th
    distinct CID carried a fragment, and its CID table was never reset
    between files. Move the tables to file scope, clear them in the
    defragment init routine, and show the fragment unreassembled with an
    expert info instead. The bs_address copy is now freed on reset.

    When the generic MAC header was reached directly, for example through
    Exported PDU, first_gmh stayed false and the reassembly ids of the
    second pass differed from the first. A direct call now counts as the
    first GMH. The new part of frag_num_array is cleared like
    cid_adj_array.

    REG-RSP decoded the whole rest of the message for every vendor
    specific, vendor id or MAC version TLV, which is quadratic. Decode only
    that TLV.

    Smaller fixes: CINR feedback in the type 2 header skipped a byte, the
    FPC station loop condition was inverted, ARQ-Discard and ARQ-Reset used
    offsets that did not account for the stripped type byte, the ARQ
    feedback IE item length was the whole message, the CID update and SA
    challenge sub-TLV loops compared an absolute offset with a length, the
    RNG-RSP sub-TLV check tested the wrong type, short HMAC tuple lengths
    and REG-RSP HMAC/CMAC offsets were wrong, UCD backoff exponents of 32
    or more shifted out of range and some UCD items had the wrong length,
    and the invalid sub-TLV items in DCD/UCD used a wrong offset and
    length.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit a29567aa46db4c1f2ade7579e06a8c8f83a922f8)

    [Backport: Needs 2f449f7335 (WiMAX: Fix some array bound overruns), picked before this commit. release-4.4 added the CINR mean and deviation as two-byte items at the same offset; took the master lines, which add each FT_UINT8 field as one byte. Kept the 4.4 abbreviation of ei_mac_crc_malformed.]

