commit 4016ba46b5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    PROFINET: Fix memory safety problems in the CBA dissectors

    A DCOM OBJREF with OXID or OID 0 creates an interface without a
    parent. cba_ldev_find() and cba_pdev_find() dereferenced the parent
    unchecked and crashed on a later CBA call to that IPID. Both now check
    for a NULL parent.

    The physical device was stored in the same private_data pointer that
    cba_ldev_find() returns as a logical device, so a get_ACCO or Connect
    request on the IPID of a physical device wrote past the end of the
    smaller structure. Both structures now start with a type tag that the
    lookups verify.

    The array sizes of Connect, Connect2, Disconnect, SRT DisconnectCR and
    SRT Connect, and the type description sizes of Connect2 and SRT Connect,
    sized allocations (up to 34 GB) and loops. They are now limited to the
    bytes remaining in the packet divided by the minimum element size, with
    an expert info. Connection tracking, whose lists are searched linearly,
    was quadratic: each logical device list and each SRT frame now keeps at
    most 5000 connections, later ones are reported with an expert info and
    not tracked. The code that fills in connection results now accepts
    connections that are not tracked.

    ICBAAccoServerSRT::ConnectCR passed hfindex 0 with a NULL tree, which
    asserts in the registrar; pass -1. The PN-RT heuristic looked up frames
    with a destination address that is not an Ethernet address, which can be
    NULL; it now requires AT_ETHER.

    DiagConsConnections responses passed an uninitialized item pointer to
    proto_item_set_text() when dissected without a tree, because
    dissect_dcom_HRESULT_item() only sets it with a tree. That crashed on
    the first pass of tshark -2. Initialize it to NULL.

    Also loop on u32ArraySize >= 2 in dissect_PBAddressInfo() so an odd
    size no longer wraps, and set qc_reported to true after the first QC
    expert info, as intended.

    The cleanup routine freed only the list of physical devices; free the
    logical device, frame and connection lists hanging off them too.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit bc8ec2c6770914cb1954d9bf4671b5b6433d87d8)

    [Backport: release-4.4 val_to_str() has no allocator argument; kept the 4.4 call where the QC expert info is reported. packet-dcom-cba-acco.h on 4.4 lacks master's Doxygen comments; added the kind tags, connection counters and cba_free_all() declaration without them.]

