commit c148f5b876
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    IrDA: Fix an XID hints over-read and decode IAP results consistently

    dissect_xid() built the service hints text by overwriting its first two
    characters with " (". When hint bits were set but none of the named
    ones, the string was just ")" and the overwrite removed its terminating
    NUL, so reading it ran off the end of the stack buffer. Append the
    hints only when at least one is named.

    dissect_iap_result() honored the list length only when building a tree,
    so the LMP conversations created by the attribute value dissectors
    depended on whether a tree existed and frames decoded differently with
    "tshark -2". Read and honor the list length in the no-tree branch too.

    add_lmp_conversation() dereferenced a NULL pointer if an existing
    conversation had no IrLMP data; allocate the data in that case. Only
    look at the IrDA pseudo-header when the encapsulation is IrDA, as it
    holds unrelated data when reached through SLL, SIR or Exported PDU.

    Make attr_len unsigned so that large octet sequence lengths do not
    wrap, and actually append the octet count to the Info column.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 098de61478015b0acf7db0e6a217d0a2e7f5af91)

commit 1ca2879ae1
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    Gryphon: Fix an endless loop and a dissection depth leak

    cmd_usdt_register_non_legacy() looped forever on a USDT register block
    whose ID count is zero, because neither the offset nor the remaining
    length advanced. Skip the 20 byte block and stop if less than 20 bytes
    remain.

    The dissection depth was incremented in dissect_gryphon_message(),
    decode_command() and decode_response() and only decremented on normal
    return. An exception in a PDU skipped the decrements, and
    tcp_dissect_pdus() goes on with the next PDU of the frame, so a frame of
    many malformed PDUs ended in the depth assertion. Restore the depth
    after each PDU.

    Also use the field offset in cmd_bits_in()/cmd_bits_out() instead of the
    constant 1, make the NUL-terminated name fields FT_STRINGZ, avoid a
    wrap of the node name count in resp_ldf_get_node_names() when it is 0,
    and loop over events only while a whole 20 byte event remains.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 8b589bc58ce4ebd640062e01e1266a6f4c4056b6)

    [Backport: added #include <epan/exceptions.h>, which master already has, for the TRY block.]

commit 7401060b13
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 15:07:07 2026 +1000

    Falco Events: Harden against packet records and failed extraction

    dissect_falco_event() is registered as a dissector and can be reached
    from Exported PDU, whose record is REC_TYPE_PACKET. It then read
    rec_header.syscall_header, a union member that overlays the packet
    header, and passed its wth field to open_sinsp_capture(), which writes
    through it. Return 0 for records that are not REC_TYPE_SYSCALL. The
    event_param_data passed as dissector data is NULL when called without
    data; check it before use in dissect_sinsp_enriched().

    extract_syscall_conversation_fields() returned before it initialised
    its output when the protocol was disabled or the capture could not be
    opened, so the conversation filter callbacks and get_fd_stream_info()
    used an uninitialised container_id. Initialise the output first. On an
    extraction failure it called REPORT_DISSECTOR_BUG() from callbacks that
    run outside dissection, where nothing catches the exception; return
    false instead.

    Check the lineage number against N_PROC_LINEAGE_ENTRIES before indexing
    lineage_trees, and check hf_id_to_addr_id for NULL before use.

    Use PRId64 for the signed tid and return NULL, not false, from
    get_fd_stream_info().

