commit 77d434c57a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:43 2026 +1000

    VNC: Fix Tight assert and several decoding errors

    A Tight rectangle whose compression control nibble is 0xA to 0xF only
    raised an expert info and left bytes_needed at -1, so the following
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT(bytes_needed != -1) fired on a malformed packet.
    Set bytes_needed to 0 after the expert info.

    vnc_client_cut_text_extended() called abs() on the length, which is
    undefined for INT_MIN. Negate in unsigned arithmetic instead. The
    original-format text was also added with length message_length - 4
    while the offset advanced by message_length; use message_length.

    vnc_server_cut_text() returned the offset as "bytes needed", which made
    the caller ask for more data after every complete message. Return 0. It
    also did not skip the 3 padding bytes after the message type, so the
    length was read from the padding and the text was decoded as the next
    message; skip them.

    SetColourMapEntries read the colour count from absolute offset 4;
    read it relative to the message start. It also asked for 3 bytes more
    than the message holds, because the bytes already consumed were counted
    again. The width * height * bpp
    products in the raw, ZRLE raw and rich cursor encodings were computed in
    signed int and could overflow; compute them in unsigned.

    On 4.4 the extended client cut text code does not exist, so only the
    other fixes are ported.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
