commit 4f522e4dfb
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 06:57:16 2026 +1000

    Z39.50: Bound RPN, element data type and GRS-1 nesting

    RPN queries (RPNStructure/rpnRpnOp), structured element data types
    (ElementDataType/structured) and GRS-1 subtrees (ElementData/subtree)
    can nest without limit. The generated code bounds these cycles only
    with increment_dissection_depth_by_n(), which asserts at the tree
    depth limit, so a search request of about 1.5 KB with 250 nested RPN
    operators on the default port ended in a dissector bug, and aborted
    under WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG. Count the nesting per packet,
    stop at 32 levels with an expert info, and leave the rest undissected.

    The MARC leader expert infos printed an invalid octet with %c, which
    puts a raw byte that may not be valid UTF-8 into the label (the fuzzer
    aborts on that). Print it in hex.

