commit b676649959
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:01 2026 +1000

    RTnet: Bound nesting of tunneled RTmac headers

    With RTmac version 2 and the tunnel flag set, the next protocol is
    looked up in the ethertype table using the packet's own type field.
    Type 0x9021 is RTmac itself, so every 4-byte header called
    dissect_rtmac() again on the rest of the frame. A small frame ran into
    the generic layer-count assertion in call_dissector(). The version 1
    default case had the same loop.

    Count the nesting per packet with p_get_proto_depth() and, beyond four
    levels, hand the rest to the data dissector instead of recursing.

