commit 93c22885e4
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:01 2026 +1000

    TNS: Fix a Data Descriptor assert and several bad reads and loops

    A Data Descriptor PDU with a header length below 8 but a non-zero data
    length passed tcp_dissect_pdus() and then hit a DISSECTOR_ASSERT_CMPINT
    on the header length. Report it with an expert info and stop instead.

    tns_format_vector() added 8 to its position for the optional header
    without checking it against the image length. The following length
    check then compared against a negative remainder converted to unsigned,
    so it passed and the loop read up to 145 bytes beyond the buffer. Return
    NULL when the position is past the end.

    A TTI_RXD row with columns that consume no bytes (NULL columns without
    a data length, or "same as previous row" columns) cost one iteration
    per column for each one-byte row, which is quadratic in the packet
    size. Count such columns per message, stop at 100000 and add an expert
    info; real result sets never reach this.

    The rendered text of OSON (JSON) values contains raw bytes from the
    packet and can be invalid UTF-8, which aborts the fuzzer. Sanitize it
    with get_utf_8_string() before it goes into the item label.

    Also check a chunk length against the remaining bytes in
    tns_chunks_len() so the offset cannot overflow, and compute the thin
    TTI_IOV bind count in unsigned arithmetic.

    On 4.4 only the Data Descriptor header length assert applies; the other
    hunks are for code that does not exist there.

