commit a776d88bfe
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:43 2026 +1000

    WCP: Fix history window wrap and the second pass dissector bug

    A packet whose decompression failed on the first pass has no stored
    data. On the second pass (tshark -2, or any redissection in the GUI)
    the checks run against the final window state, can pass, and then
    REPORT_DISSECTOR_BUG("Can't find uncompressed data") fired, aborting
    under WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG. Make the checks that depend on
    the window state only on the first pass, record a failure with its
    expert info, and show the same expert info at the same point on later
    passes, so that tshark -2 gives the same result as one pass.

    The history window wrap test compared the pointer before incrementing
    it, so the write pointer could reach the end of the buffer and the next
    byte was written to buffer[MAX_WIN_BUF_LEN], one past the array. Wrap
    after incrementing, in decompressed_entry() and for literal bytes. A
    packet that ends exactly at the end of the window now leaves buf_cur at
    the start of the window instead of getting stuck.

    wcp_save_data() had an unreachable wrap branch and underflowed the
    length for packets shorter than 3 bytes. Reject short packets and
    lengths larger than the window, and copy in two pieces when the data
    wraps.

    On release-4.4 the offsets are int and proto_tree_add_expert_remaining()
    does not exist, so the equivalent calls are used.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
