commit a49ef81c2d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UCP: Fix a dissector bug in 23R and some length handling

    add_23R() dissected the IVR5x field, which is an FT_STRING, with
    UcpHandleByte(), which uses proto_tree_add_uint(). This reported a
    dissector bug (an abort when WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG is set)
    for a packet found by the default heuristic when a tree is built. Use
    UcpHandleString() as add_23O() does.

    tvb_ensure_bytes_exist() was passed the absolute end offset as a
    length; pass the length from the current offset. In check_ucp() the
    loop bound "length - 2" wrapped when the ETX was at offset 1; compare
    as "offset + 2 < length".

    On release-4.4 the tvb_ensure_bytes_exist() calls already use the right
    length, so only the check_ucp() loop bound and the 23R IVR5x handling
    are ported.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
