commit c35dddb67c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 06:57:17 2026 +1000

    ZigBee Security: Fix uninitialised PAN and bound the NWK key ring

    For an APS relay downstream message without an 802.15.4 layer (ZigBee
    Direct over Bluetooth) addr16.pan was never set but was hashed in the
    short address lookup, giving a nondeterministic source address. Zero
    the structure and use the PAN of the NWK hints in that case.

    The NWK key ring only compared a new key against the head of the list,
    so each Transport-Key packet with a distinct key grew the ring and
    every secured frame tried all keys (4000 keys x 4000 frames took 7
    seconds). Compare against the whole ring and keep at most 64 keys per
    PAN; keys beyond that are ignored with a new expert info, which is
    remembered per frame so that later passes report it too.

    On release-4.4 only zbee_sec_add_key_to_keyring() exists (no _panid
    variant), and the proto data uses proto_get_id_by_filter_name() as the
    rest of the file does.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit c241e4bf6946cd81a25ef45aea25b10f8493df9e)

commit 8551418a13
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    Telnet: Fix IAC search, NULL suboption tvb and length underflows

    find_unescaped_iac() never reported "not found" since abbe56cd76:
    tvb_find_uint8_length() leaves the offset at the end of the data, so
    dissect_telnet() always called telnet_command() past the end and every
    packet without an IAC was marked Malformed. It also made the TN3270 and
    TN5250 "one more segment" path unreachable. Return a bool with an
    output offset, and treat an IAC in the last byte as a command instead of
    throwing while looking at the next byte.

    unescape_and_tvbuffify_telnet_option() returns NULL for suboptions of
    10240 bytes or more. telnet_sub_option() passed that NULL tvb to the
    suboption dissector or to proto_tree_add_item(), which asserts. Add an
    expert info and return instead.

    Fix length handling in suboption dissectors: AUTHENTICATION SEND with an
    odd length (loop now runs while at least 2 bytes remain), the
    authentication data length underflow when fewer than 2 bytes are left,
    and the TN3270E CONNECT, IS, REASON and FUNCTIONS requests, which used
    a length that extended one byte past the suboption or wrapped the
    remaining length when it was fully consumed.

    On release-4.4 find_unescaped_iac() still returns an int with -1 for not
    found, so only the IAC-in-the-last-byte case is fixed there, and the
    tvb_find_uint8() length is adjusted instead of tvb_find_uint8_length().

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit eff4b8be43a81cf5959ead014d18b4c5ac873bd7)

commit ae5bae5455
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:28 2026 +1000

    SSH: Fix aborts and over-reads in key exchange and key setup

    A stale mac_id (hmac-sha2-256 negotiated in an earlier key exchange)
    made ssh_derive_symmetric_keys() overwrite the 64 bytes needed by
    chacha20 with 32. ssh_decryption_setup_cipher() then copied 64 bytes
    from a 32-byte key. Only raise "need" to 32, and copy the chacha20
    key only if at least 64 bytes were derived.

    ssh_kex_shared_secret() asserted on a missing public or private key
    and passed a zero or one modulus from a DH group exchange to
    gcry_mpi_powm(), which aborts the process with a divide by zero. Return
    NULL for a missing key and for a modulus <= 1; the caller already
    handles NULL.

    ssh_set_mac_length() accepted any -<bits> suffix, so a MAC length
    larger than DIGEST_MAX_SIZE (48 bytes) led to an over-read of calc_mac.
    Reject MAC lengths above DIGEST_MAX_SIZE.

    ssh_read_e_pq() and ssh_read_f_pq() returned false on an invalid
    length, but the callers test for < 0, so the expert info was never
    shown. Return -1. Also set the offset after the protocol banner to
    the next line start instead of adding it to the offset.

    On release-4.4 the banner offset and PQ key readers (ssh_read_e_pq/f_pq)
    are not applicable, and only the chacha20 key length check is ported to
    ssh_decryption_setup_cipher().

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit e2064591c19a34592fc07a2626a9e851dad422d3)

commit ec1f7e8c1a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:02 2026 +1000

    SCYLLA: Fix an endless loop and an uninitialized response frame

    dissect_scylla_negotiation_pdu() loops while the unsigned remaining
    length is non-zero and subtracts a feature length taken from the packet
    without checking it. A feature length such as 0xfffffff8 for
    CONNECTION_ID moved the offset back by exactly the header size on each
    pass while the length stayed unchanged, so tshark looped forever.

    Loop only while a full 8 byte feature header remains and stop with a
    new malformed expert info when the feature length exceeds the remaining
    negotiation data.

    The request and response map entry was allocated with wmem_new() and
    response_frame_num was never set for a request whose response does
    not arrive, so later passes read an uninitialized value and showed a
    random "Response frame" link. Allocate it with wmem_new0().

    On release-4.4 only the wmem_new0() change is applicable; the
    negotiation feature loop does not exist there.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit a691cee366fa0071d122e37a4d95e2de793c5671)

commit 35b1ad66f1
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 17 16:54:10 2026 +1000

    RESP: Fix an out-of-bounds read in the JSON detection

    When a string is inside a request array and looks like JSON, the
    dissector indexed the string with the length declared in the packet and
    built the JSON tvbuff with that length, but the string was read with the
    number of bytes actually captured. A snaplen-truncated frame declaring a
    huge length read far past the buffer and crashed; a verbatim string read
    two bytes past it even in a complete packet. Use the length actually
    read.

    A declared string length is now clamped to INT_MAX - 4, so adding the
    CRLF length can no longer overflow, and the 64-bit value is no longer
    truncated to int.

    The verbatim string value skipped the encoding and the colon but was one
    byte too long, including the CR. Use captured - 4, and require at least
    4 bytes before reading the encoding.

    Bulk errors used the bulk string fields; use the registered bulk error
    fields.

    On release-4.4 only the clamp of the declared bulk string length is
    applicable; the JSON detection and RESP3 code do not exist there.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 228f3d334163e098a5da7745d1c0e1f20caf2c11)

