commit 6a6f0b4d58
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 23:07:16 2026 -0400

    BLF: Check the APP_TEXT length against the object length

    The text length in an APP_TEXT object was used to allocate a buffer
    (up to 4 GiB) before checking that the text fits in the object. This
    displays bytes from adjacent containers and is not a security issue,
    but does indicate a malformed file. Reject the object if the text is
    longer than the rest of the object.

    Thanks to AISLE Security and Simon Huang for separately reporting this
    issue.

    Fix #21770

