commit 2c890bef68
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 07:03:04 2026 -0500

    Qt: Ensure that the packet list items are vertically center aligned

    A QItemView by default falls back to Qt::AlignLeft | Qt::AlignVCenter
    if Qt::TextAlignmentMode returns an invalid QVariant(). If we return
    only a horizontal text alignment flag, it does *not* use the default
    vertical alignment of Qt::AlignVCenter, but aligns with the top edge.
    Note that Qt::AlignCenter is a two-dimensional flag, hence setting it
    also aligned the text vertically in the center.

    Ping #21735

    https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qt.html#AlignmentFlag-enum

    (backported from commit ab5ad1acb47632f2f17294cacec1c9ee3c281143,
    and slightly changed to work on Qt 5.)

commit ecf428062a
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 09:07:14 2026 -0500

    charsets: Fix Windows-1252 0x8E and 0x9E

    The cp1252 table, added in commit 03c5da8d89 ("Add Windows code page
    1252."), mapped 0x8E/0x9E to U+0172/U+0173 (LATIN CAPITAL/SMALL LETTER
    U WITH OGONEK, Lithuanian letters) instead of U+017D/U+017E (LATIN
    CAPITAL/SMALL LETTER Z WITH CARON, Czech/Slovak letters) from the
    Microsoft mapping the table documents as its source:

        https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP1252.TXT

        0x8E    0x017D    #LATIN CAPITAL LETTER Z WITH CARON
        0x9E    0x017E    #LATIN SMALL LETTER Z WITH CARON

    The table is used for display only, through tvb_get_string_enc() and
    tvb_get_stringz_enc() with ENC_WINDOWS_1252: the MySQL dissector decodes
    result-set and query text with it (MySQL's "latin1" is CP1252) and the
    TNEF dissector falls back to it.  After this fix those strings show
    Z with caron where they previously showed the Unicode REPLACEMENT
    CHARACTER; nothing else changes.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: 3j27 <3j27@proton.me>

