commit 5a3724571e
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 23:02:13 2026 -0500

    ERF: Support writing with CLI tools

    Since editcap and tshark started adding the IDBs of the input file
    with wtap_dump_add_idb() (d0270415a9), writing an ERF file from the
    command line has failed on the first record with "Adding IDBs isn't
    supported by this file type", even with tshark -2. Writing from the
    GUI works because it passes all the IDBs when opening the file.

    wtap_dump_add_idb() adds the IDB to wdh->interface_data, from which
    the ERF writer takes the interface information when it builds the
    metadata record, so adding a stub that returns true is sufficent to
    work as well as it did before the above commit; slightly better even
    for IDBs that appear mid-file.

    A proper fix would involve doing work in erf_add_idb to properly
    give interfaces sources and names, and pulling some of the code
    out from where it is scattered. That's probably too much to backport.

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 verified the solution

    (cherry picked from commit 284ca34b210ef82ac2fd86e595d1c51514c5b36b)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

commit 969cd15428
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:38:28 2026 +1000

    ELF: Fix assertions, an endless loop and quadratic memory use

    value_guard() asserted on any file offset or size above INT_MAX. These
    values come from the file, so throw ReportedBoundsError instead.

    An eh_frame_hdr whose binary search table encoding has length zero (for
    example DW_EH_PE_omit) never advanced the offset in the table loop, and
    the 32-bit entry counter wrapped for counts of 2^32 or more. Return when
    the entry length is not positive and use a 64-bit counter.

    Symbol and section names were copied from the string table without a
    length limit for every symbol and section, so many entries pointing at
    one very long string used quadratic memory. Fetch names through a helper
    that reads at most 256 bytes.

    Also read a 2 byte FDE count as 16 bits, compute the trailing blackhole
    size from offset plus size, and attach the invalid data encoding and
    program and section header entry size expert infos to their own items.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit ca86e4571b9d4c0d5e6e838bf6ffdaf3f081e16f)
    [Backport: 4.4 reads the header fields with explicit byte order tests
    and lacks the invalid class, data encoding and entry size expert infos;
    applied the value_guard(), name length cap, eh_frame_hdr loop and
    blackhole size changes only. The 2 byte FDE count was already read as
    16 bits.]

commit bbb62cbf7f
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:38:28 2026 +1000

    BLF: Bound log container handling

    A LOG_CONTAINER whose object length was smaller than its headers made
    the payload length negative. The sub-tvb then ran to the end of the
    file, the loop bound wrapped, and the function returned a length that
    made the outer scan dissect the following container again. Chained
    containers doubled the work each time (exponential memory and CPU).
    Report an expert info and stop when the object length is too short,
    and use the computed payload length for the sub-tvb, the payload item
    and the loop bound; the latter now uses the length of the decompressed
    data instead of the compressed length.

    Compressed containers found inside a container are no longer
    decompressed (a double zlib stream amplified about a million times).
    This adds the blf.nested_container expert info.

    Also fix the header date: the month is 1-based for mktime(), and the
    weekday name and printed fields now use the raw values instead of the
    normalized struct tm.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 683a9baeabab14b85cc1b2611f87d3b575541372)
    [Backport: 4.4 has no frame_number argument in the BLF object
    functions; added only the in_container argument. 4.4 shows the header
    date with proto_tree_add_bytes_format() from the raw values, so the
    header date change is not needed.]

commit 8f9988f626
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 14:17:12 2026 +1000

    BER: Check the field before adding an empty bit string

    dissect_ber_constrained_bitstring() checks hf_id before adding the item
    for a bit string with content, but not for an empty one (a length of 1
    with a zero pad octet). A caller that passes -1 because it adds the
    bits itself, as LI_XER does for the NCI, then hit the "Unregistered hf"
    assertion on a packet with an empty bit string. Add the item only for
    a registered field, as the other path does.

