commit 6168ad0434
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:38:28 2026 +1000

    RFC 7468: Allocate the base64 decode buffer once

    The decode buffer was grown with wmem_realloc() on the packet pool for
    every base64 line. On that pool realloc allocates and copies and free is
    a no-op, so memory use was quadratic in the number of lines (100000
    lines exhausted memory). The decoded data is never larger than 3/4 of
    the remaining input plus a few bytes for the decoder state, so the
    buffer is now allocated once, before the loop.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit fa45c16a96d27298c076424c00becd1cb1832a41)

