commit 01ffde38b4
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:38:28 2026 +1000

    JPEG: Follow each EXIF extension IFD pointer type only once

    Every ExifIFDPointer, GPS or Interoperability pointer entry in an IFD
    started a full walk of the IFD it pointed to. Pointers can repeat or
    point back at IFD0, so a 64 KB APP1 segment cost about 29 million IFD
    entries and several segments added up. Each of the three extension
    types is now followed at most once per TIFF structure (tracked in a
    bitmask passed down the IFD chain); further pointers get an expert info.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit dd4a9f5c777584440717acd403de5fb5a0bbd3d2)

