commit 48c7f784b6
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UDPCP: Do not abort on a missing conversation

    On the first pass the dissector looked up the conversation with
    find_conversation() and passed the result to
    conversation_get_proto_data() without checking it. When no UDP dissector
    had created a conversation, for example when the dissector is reached
    through Exported PDU, the lookup returned NULL and REPORT_DISSECTOR_BUG
    aborted. Use find_or_create_conversation() on the first pass, and on
    later passes stop dissecting the conversation state if no conversation
    is found.

    Also add the missing closing parenthesis to the "No ACK seen" and "No SN
    frame seen" expert info texts.

