commit 80ac05cc37
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:36:49 2026 +1000

    epan: Stop at the protocol layer depth limit without asserting

    call_dissector_work() asserted that the number of protocol layers is
    below gui.max_tree_depth. Encapsulations that can contain themselves
    can nest without limit in a crafted packet: 600 IPv4-in-IPv4 headers
    on raw IP, or TZSP carrying raw IP to the TZSP UDP port again (about
    125 levels in one 4 KB frame), reached the assertion with default
    settings, and the test suite and the fuzzer abort on it with
    WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG. That is bad packet data, not a
    dissector bug. Throw a DissectorError with a message instead, as the
    tree depth limit in proto.c does.

