commit 144143d559
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 06:57:17 2026 +1000

    ZigBee APS: Bound recursion through nested tunnel commands

    An APS Tunnel command hands the rest of the frame back to the APS
    dissector, which can be another Tunnel command. Each level costs only
    11 bytes, so a large frame nests hundreds of levels until
    call_dissector_work() hits its layers assertion and aborts.

    Count the nesting per packet with p_get_proto_depth() and stop at 4
    levels with a new expert info (zbee_aps.tunnel_depth) instead of
    dissecting the inner frame.

