commit fa19d3625c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TCAP: Bound parameter nesting and the SRT chain length

    dissect_tcap_param() recursed on nested constructors without a limit
    other than increment_dissection_depth(), which asserts at the limit.
    A packet with a few hundred nested constructors in a component that no
    subdissector handles aborts.  Pass a nesting level and stop after 16
    levels with the new expert info tcap.param_too_deep.

    The service response time matching walked the whole chain of begin
    transactions with the same transaction ID for every packet, which is
    quadratic when a capture reuses one OTID with more than the lost-message
    timeout between Begins.  Stop at 1000 entries in a chain, add the new
    expert info tcap.srt_chain_too_long and skip SRT matching for those
    packets.

    Also use unsigned for the length of the originating and destination
    transaction IDs, which was truncated to 8 bits.

