commit 5cbdbac26a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:28 2026 +1000

    SPNEGO: Bound nesting of SPNEGO tokens

    A NegTokenInit can list SPNEGO itself as a mechanism and carry another
    SPNEGO token as its mechToken, which is then passed back to the SPNEGO
    dissector.  An InnerContextToken handled by spnego-wrap can loop the
    same way.  A packet of a few kilobytes nests several hundred levels and
    ends in the dissection depth assertion in packet.c.

    Keep a per-packet nesting counter with p_get_proto_depth() in
    dissect_spnego() and dissect_spnego_wrap().  Beyond 8 levels, add the
    new expert info spnego.too_deep and stop.

