commit 9750e6ec64
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TECMP: Restore pkt_len when the Ethernet dissector throws

    dissect_ethernet_payload() overwrites the persistent pinfo->fd->pkt_len
    while the Ethernet dissector runs and restored it afterwards only if no
    exception was thrown. After a short or malformed Ethernet entry the
    frame kept the reduced length, so later dissection passes saw a wrong
    frame.len and a bogus "Frame length is less than captured length"
    error. Restore the value in a FINALLY block.

    The FR POC State and 10BASE-T1S control messages named the interface
    with an interface_id that was never set, so it was always 0. Read the
    value from the packet. The CAN Replay Fill Level message advanced the
    offset one byte too far after the queue loop, which made the returned
    length and the TECMP item one byte too long. Zero-initialise
    tecmp_info in dissect_data() so subdissectors never see an
    uninitialised data_flags.

