commit 6a8f346417
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:02 2026 +1000

    SMB: Bound export object memory for sparse files

    insert_chunk() sized the export object buffer to the file offset plus
    length of each chunk, up to 4 GiB, and zeroed all of it. Two small
    packets writing at offset 0 and at 0xFFFFFF00 of the same FID made
    tshark allocate and touch about 4 GiB. A chunk that would grow the
    buffer by more than 64 MiB beyond the data gathered so far is now
    treated like an allocation failure, so the file is marked out of memory.

    Also stop Write AndX from wrapping the 16-bit data offset when it skips
    the pipe write length, and clamp the NT_TRANS_CREATE extended attribute
    length to the data that is left, so that 0xFFFFFFFF is no longer taken
    as -1 (to end of tvb).

