commit 93cb149928
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:01 2026 +1000

    SCTP: Bound the fragments stored per message

    Reassembly of unordered DATA chunks put every fragment of a stream
    into one message, because the stream sequence number is forced to 0.
    Each new fragment costs two walks of the fragment list, so a capture
    with many unordered middle fragments took quadratic time. Store at
    most 1024 fragments per message; later ones are not reassembled and
    get an expert info and a Info column note.

    The SACK chunk made the cumulative TSN ack relative to the first TSN
    for display and then passed that value to sctp_ack_block(), which
    subtracts the first TSN again, so SACKs never marked DATA chunks as
    acknowledged with relative TSNs on (the default). Pass the raw
    cumulative TSN to sctp_ack_block() and use the relative value only for
    display, as the NR-SACK code already does.

    The tap was queued in a FINALLY clause even when the chunks threw an
    exception, and the taps read the chunk tvbs outside of any TRY block.
    A chunk of length 0 made tshark -z sctp,stat abort with an unhandled
    exception. Queue the tap only when the packet was dissected completely.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 83577f306268cea942c1e909db94c91ac3f629ab)

commit 43924c3a83
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:01 2026 +1000

    SAP Router: Stop routed messages from dissecting themselves

    A route whose last hop names the SAP Router port (3298 or 3299) made
    the Routed message branch look the destination port up in the sapni.port
    table, which found SAP Router again. It ran on the same data at offset
    0 in the same conversation, reached the same branch and recursed until
    the layer limit failed a DISSECTOR_ASSERT.

    Do not hand the payload to the sub-dissector when the destination port
    is in the SAP Router port range, report an expert info instead, and wrap
    the nested call in increment_dissection_depth() and
    decrement_dissection_depth().

