commit 66c24a5989
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 22:31:19 2026 +1000

    RNSAP: Do not add a protocol layer per IE, and bound IE nesting

    Every protocol IE and extension was dispatched through its dissector
    table with dissector_try_uint(), which adds an "rnsap" entry to the
    frame's protocol layers each time. A PDU with a few hundred IEs (or
    nested extension containers) reached the layer limit and failed the
    assertion in call_dissector_work() ("saved_layers_len <
    prefs.gui_max_tree_depth"), a dissector bug triggered by the packet;
    with WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG set, tshark aborted.

    Dispatch the IEs without adding a layer, as RANAP, S1AP and X2AP do,
    and since that no longer limits recursion, bound the nesting of IEs and
    extensions to 32 per packet with an expert info.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    [4.4: dissector_try_uint_with_data() is called dissector_try_uint_new() here.]

