commit c6014f127b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RSVD: Fix a dissector bug on every SRB status response

    The SRB status response branch added the SrbStatus field with
    proto_tree_add_bits_item(), but the field has a 0x7f bitmask. The bits
    API reports a dissector bug for a field with a bitmask, so every
    RSVD_TUNNEL_SRB_STATUS response raised an exception when a tree was
    built (and aborts with WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_DISSECTOR_BUG). Use
    proto_tree_add_item(), which applies the mask.

    The length passed to the sub-dissectors was truncated to 16 bits and
    could go negative for tunnelled SCSI data over 32 KB. Use int.

