commit ac1721722b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RSVP: Bound the Juniper TLV loop, drop the unused request hash

    The JUNIPER_PROPERTIES object loop ran the packet's 16-bit TLV count
    without regard to the object length, so each object re-walked all the
    bytes after it, which is quadratic in the packet size (about 1.3 s per
    64 KB datagram). A TLV length below 2 also moved the offset backwards.
    Stop at the end of the object and report a TLV length below 2, or one
    that runs past the object, with an expert info.

    The request hash was keyed on the conversation index only, so all keys
    between one address pair shared a bucket and every packet walked the
    whole chain. Nothing ever read the hash value, so remove the hash, its
    key and value structures and the conversation lookup that only fed it.

    Small decoding fixes: compare the upstream label with a 32-bit value;
    print the P2MP IPv6 sender with tvb_ip6_to_str() and read the Sub-Group
    ID at the right offset; make the 3GPP2 Profile ID a 16-bit field and
    read Max_Latency, Max_Loss_Rate and Delay_Var_Sensitive with the widths
    they are advanced by; reject a 3GPP2 QoS list length below 2 instead of
    letting it wrap; skip the data of unknown 3GPP2 information elements;
    advance GENERALIZED_UNI sub-objects by their 16-bit length and read the
    egress label direction at the right offset.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 890608bba54499201e9f8efa4de199bab5681362)

commit 596b7bcb92
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 21:58:02 2026 -0500

    PKCS12: Don't use a stale or NULL OID for EncryptedData

    The EncryptedData footer passed the file-scope object_identifier_id
    to dissector_change_string(), dissector_reset_string() and
    PBE_decrypt_data(). That pointer is allocated from the packet pool and
    is only set by a SafeBag, CertBag, CRLBag, SecretBag or PKCS12Attribute
    earlier in the dissection, but EncryptedPrivateKeyInfo is also
    registered for pkcs-9-at-encryptedPrivateKeyInfo and can be reached
    without one. The OID was then NULL, crashing in g_str_hash(), or
    pointed into the pool of an earlier packet.

    Remember the bag OID in per-packet proto data and skip the temporary
    dissector swap and decryption when there is none.

    This code was removed from later releases when the PKCS #8 structures
    moved to the AKP dissector (3b74ede300).

    Assisted-by: Claude

