commit 83dca4f755
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:44 2026 +1000

    X11: Fix modifier map OOB read and keysym assert

    A truncated GetModifierMapping reply or SetModifierMapping request
    left the conversation with a large keycodes_per_modifier and the old,
    smaller modifiermap arrays, so the next KeyPress read past the arrays.
    listOfKeycode() now builds the arrays locally and commits them only
    when the whole list was read, and the callers store
    keycodes_per_modifier only after that.

    A GetKeyboardMapping reply with a huge reply length stored the length
    in a signed int and tripped DISSECTOR_ASSERT(keycode_count >= 0). Use
    an unsigned length, clamp the keycode count to 256 and report invalid
    counts with an expert info instead of an assertion.

    A ChangeKeyboardMapping with keysyms_per_keycode 0 created an empty
    keysym array whose first element keycode2keysymString() read
    uninitialized. Reject it in listOfKeysyms() and return "<Unknown>" for
    an empty array.

    Also fix small decoding bugs: the arc width, height and angles were
    all shown with the y value, arc and color item lists were 12 bytes per
    item but sized as 8, consistentWithOrder() and the opcode check used
    absolute offsets instead of offsets relative to the request, and the
    keysym selection for the Lock case used a stale value instead of
    syms[1].

