commit 28c10b2ebc
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:44 2026 +1000

    WTP: Refuse nested concatenated PDUs

    A concatenated PDU (first byte 0) was dissected by recursing into
    dissect_wtp_common() for every sub-PDU, and a sub-PDU could itself be a
    concatenated PDU. Each level needs only 2-3 bytes, so one packet could
    nest about 10900 levels deep, which is a stack exhaustion risk when no
    tree is built. The specification does not allow a concatenated PDU
    inside another one, so a nested one is now reported with a new expert
    info (wtp.nested_concat) and not dissected. Recursion depth is thus at
    most one level.

    Also pass ENC_NA instead of the packet byte as the encoding of the
    continue flag item.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
