commit b793bf10c8
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:44 2026 +1000

    WLCCP: Bound TLV nesting and stop asserting on sibling count

    dissect_wlccp_tlvs() recursed with "_depth++", which passes the
    parent's current value and increments the parent's counter once per
    child. The counter therefore counted siblings, not nesting: a container
    with 101 child TLVs hit DISSECTOR_ASSERT(_depth < 100), while nested
    containers always got depth 0 and were not bounded at all, so about
    700 levels of 8 byte TLVs reached the tree depth limit.

    Pass _depth + 1 to the child and stop with a new expert info
    (wlccp.tlv_too_deep) at a nesting level of 32. The function now takes
    pinfo. The "offset > old_offset" asserts become loop exits.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 5585326710ebe5ceb13599ebee6514753a65cde7)

commit 4abc016918
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 13:32:44 2026 +1000

    SMB: Bound conditional ACE nesting and SRA value counts

    A conditional ACE could nest COMPOSITE tokens about 13000 levels deep
    (five bytes each), reaching the tree depth limit and a dissector bug
    assertion. Pass a nesting level down and stop with an expert info at
    32 levels.

    The SYSTEM_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTE ACE did not check its value count or
    value offsets against the ACE size, so many offsets pointing at one
    long string cost O(N*S) time and memory. Cap the value count by what
    the ACE can hold (size / 4) and skip value offsets beyond the ACE,
