commit 5484468a96
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    USB HID: Bound Collection nesting, report sizes and usage expansion

    A report descriptor made of Collection items nested more deeply than
    the tree depth limit reached an assertion in the recursive item
    dissector. Nesting is now limited to 32 levels; beyond that an expert
    info is added and the rest of the descriptor is skipped.

    A Report Size above 32 bits, or a report_size * report_count above
    65535 * 8 bits (computed in 64 bits), is now rejected when the
    descriptor is parsed. Sizes above 64 bits made the bit item functions
    report a dissector bug, and the 32-bit product of an array field could
    wrap and let the per-element loop run about four billion times.

    Usage ranges were limited per field only, so a short descriptor could
    allocate hundreds of megabytes of file-scope memory. The expanded
    usages of one descriptor are now limited to 131072 in total.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit baa7f9374fd373e6b11e12c04eea23ce146d94d3)

commit 6f15757f54
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    USB: Fix FreeBSD empty composite assert and SET_INTERFACE slowdown

    A FreeBSD control transfer with two or more zero-length data frames
    counted each of them, but tvb_composite_append() drops empty members, so
    the composite had no members and tvb_composite_finalize() failed its
    assertion. Count only frames that contribute data.

    Every INTERFACE descriptor appended an entry to the interface's
    alternate settings array, and every SET_INTERFACE request scanned the
    whole array, which made dissection quadratic in the file size. Keep one
    entry per bAlternateSetting, which bounds the array at 256 entries.

    A string descriptor request with wLength below 2 made the string length
    wrap to 254 or 255 and the packet was reported as malformed. Use a
    length of 0 in that case.

