commit bad7438cdd
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UMTS RLC: Bound RB id, duplicate history and reassembly channels

    The radio bearer id from the packet indexed the RRC ciphering
    tables (31 entries) unchecked in is_ciphered_according_to_rrc() and
    rlc_decipher(), a heap read past the end with RLC over UDP. Ids of
    31 or more are now treated as not ciphered and skipped.

    rlc_is_duplicate() kept every PDU of a channel in a list searched
    linearly for each PDU, so the cost grew quadratically (40000 frames
    took 32 s). The history is now capped at 1024 entries per channel
    (the SN window is 1024 for AM, so real traffic does not reach it),
    oldest first, and the list is only modified on the first pass.

    Each new channel allocated a 32 KiB reassembly table. The number of
    channels with such a table is now capped at 1024; further channels
    are not reassembled.

    get_reassembled_data() looked up with an uninitialised channel when
    the channel assignment failed; rlc_frag_assign() now returns the
    result and the caller gives up.

    The incomplete-sequence check now handles SN wrap-around, and the
    fragment list print no longer wraps for a zero-length fragment.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
