commit 72fcb0abc9
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UMTS MAC: Reject HS-DSCH C/T 15 and harden MAC-is reassembly

    An HS-DSCH PDU with the C/T field set to 15 gives logical channel
    id 16, which indexes lchId_type_table and lchId_rlc_map (16 entries)
    one past the end. Report the reserved value with an expert info and
    discard the PDU, as RACH and FACH already do.

    MAC-is reassembly asserted on a duplicate head, middle or tail
    segment for the same TSN and on an impossible SS/SDU combination;
    both now add an expert info and discard the segment. find_head and
    find_tail looped forever when every TSN slot held a middle segment;
    they now stop after MAX_TSN steps. The TSN is read with
    tvb_get_bits16() so a 14 bit TSN no longer fails an assertion, and
    the fragment data is copied before the fragment is linked so a
    throwing copy cannot leave uninitialised data behind.

    The C-RNTI was added to the tree from a fixed bit offset 4 instead
    of the current bit offset.

