commit dc230cafe7
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UMTS FP: Fix PCH assertion and paging indication bitmap over-read

    update_pch_conversation_info() asserted that the conversation channel
    is PCH. fp_info from FP Hint, DCT2000 or K12 need not match the
    conversation found by address and port, so a crafted Exported PDU file
    reached the assertion. Return when the conversation is not a PCH one or
    has no channel specific info.

    The relevant paging indication bitmap was stored with the length of the
    frame that carried it and shown with the length of a later frame, which
    could be longer (heap over-read) or zero (NULL data, assertion in
    tvb_get_ptr). Store the bitmap length with the bitmap, and show the
    bitmap only if it exists, using the stored length.

    The NBAP lchId tables have 16 entries but the fake logical channel id,
    which starts at 5 and grows for every new transport channel id, was
    used as an index without a bound. Use 0 for ids of 16 or more.

    The RACH new IE present flags were set whenever the division matched,
    not from the flag bit; take them from the bit. fp.hsdsch-interval and
    fp.pusch-duration hold values up to 2550 and are now FT_UINT16. The
    calculated HS-DSCH rate used integer division that gave 0 for
    intervals above 100; compute it in 64 bits and clamp to 32 bits.

