commit 083d2a3e26
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 14:44:02 2026 +1000

    UAVCAN-CAN: Fix a NULL dereference when a frame is dissected again

    In a multi-frame transfer, a frame without the start-of-transfer bit
    is skipped on the first pass when its transfer has not been seen yet.
    Such a frame gets no per-frame data. A later start frame with the same
    transfer id creates the transfer, so on the next pass (tshark -2, or
    the GUI redissecting) the earlier frame was accepted, took the visited
    branch, and dereferenced the missing per-frame data. Decide on later
    passes as the first pass did: accept a multi-frame frame only if it has
    per-frame data, and also return if that data is missing.

    A reassembled payload shorter than the two-byte CRC made the CRC
    offset and length wrap. Add an expert info and skip the CRC and DSDL
    dissection in that case.

