commit 870aa8e904
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 06:57:17 2026 +1000

    ZigBee ZCL: Bound ARRAY/SET/BAG nesting and fix structured write offsets

    An ARRAY, SET or BAG attribute value can have an element type that is
    itself an ARRAY, SET or BAG, and each level costs only three bytes.
    The dissection recursed without a bound until the proto tree depth
    limit ended it with a "Dissector bug" error. Limit the nesting to 16
    levels with a per-packet counter (p_get_proto_depth()) and add an
    expert info, zbee_zcl.too_deep, when the limit is reached.

    Write Attributes Structured and its response read the selector
    indicator and the indexes at offset 0 instead of the current offset,
    so they showed the frame control byte and misaligned what followed.
    Use *offset.

    The Command Identifiers subtree of the Discover Commands Received and
    Generated responses had the negative length *offset - tvb_len. Use
    tvb_len - *offset and drop the meaningless loop bound. The minimum and
