commit 8e095b83c5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 06:57:17 2026 +1000

    ZigBee NWK GP: Bound the key ring and fix length handling

    Every Commissioning and Commissioning Reply frame carrying a key
    prepended a record to the global key ring on every pass, with no
    duplicate check. Each fully encrypted frame tries every key, so N such
    frames and M encrypted frames cost N x M AES-CCM* decryptions per pass
    (117 s for 16000 each), and the ring grew again on each redissection.
    Use one helper at all four sites that adds a key only on the first
    pass, skips a key already anywhere in the ring and stops adding when
    the ring holds 256 keys, with a new expert info
    (zbee_nwk_gp.keyring_full), remembered per frame so that later passes
    report it too.

    The payload length was a uint8_t, so a 256 byte payload was reported
    as missing and longer ones were truncated. Make it unsigned and check
    that the payload exists before subtracting. The Read Attributes loop
    used a uint8_t counter that wraps for a list length of 255 and read
    one identifier too many for odd lengths; use an unsigned counter and
    require a full identifier. The heuristic now checks that the first
    byte exists before reading it.

