commit 67fc15ad64
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TLS: Fix handshake reassembly asserts and CPU blow-ups

    A ClientHello followed by a handshake fragment in the same record made
    the reassembly key (which contained the packet direction, recomputed
    after ssl_set_server() changed the server address) disagree with the
    reassembly id, so the next fragment hit DISSECTOR_ASSERT(fh). The
    reassembly ids are unique, so the table now compares the id only.

    The CCS frame numbers were updated on every pass. A later pass could
    therefore treat a partial handshake message as plaintext that the first
    pass had considered encrypted, and fail DISSECTOR_ASSERT(frag_info).
