commit 87198cce82
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    Thrift: Stop at the nesting limit in the binary protocol

    When the nesting limit (default 25) was reached, the generic
    TBinaryProtocol dissect_thrift_binary_linear() and
    dissect_thrift_binary_struct() returned THRIFT_SUBDISSECTOR_ERROR
    without advancing the offset. Their callers only treat
    THRIFT_REQUEST_REASSEMBLY as an error, so a list at the limit with
    elements of type list, set, map or struct and a count of up to
    0x7fffffff looped on the same offset, adding an expert info on each
    pass. A single small packet could use gigabytes of memory and a lot of
    CPU time. Return THRIFT_REQUEST_REASSEMBLY like the compact protocol
    functions do, so the callers stop.

    For the old, non-strict binary message header the message type was read
    at offset + length field + name length, although the offset was already
    past the length and the name. Read it at the offset.

