commit 2c03eb89c2
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TFTP: Fix Export Objects invalid free and reachable assertion

    In Export Objects, a later pass could keep using the file-scope wmem
    buffer left over from the first pass and hand it to the tap, which
    releases it with g_free(). That is an invalid free and corrupts the
    heap. Always keep the payload buffer in file scope and always give the
    tap a copy.

    A second transfer in one conversation that is larger than the first
    tripped DISSECTOR_ASSERT_CMPINT() on the payload offset. Check the
    bounds instead and drop the inconsistent object.

    Also make the heuristic dissector fall back to the conversation if
    none was stored on an earlier pass.

    The filename and payload copies were made in the dissector and freed
    by the Export Objects tap callback, so they leaked whenever the queued
    tap data was not delivered, as in the first pass of tshark -2. Pass
    pointers to the dissector's memory and make the copies in the tap
    callback.

