commit dc56b863c9
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TDS: Fix an endless loop in ALL_HEADERS and several decoding errors

    dissect_tds_all_headers() added the 32-bit header length from the
    packet to the unsigned offset without a check. A length such as
    0xFFFFFFF8 wrapped the offset back to an earlier header, so the loop
    never ended and burned CPU on a single SQL batch packet. Reject a
    header length that runs past the ALL_HEADERS length, and a total
    length smaller than its own 4 byte field.

    Small decoding fixes:

    The decision whether a packet goes through in-order reassembly was
    taken from a flag that is set while dissecting, so a second pass
    could choose differently and show a single-buffer packet as Data.
    Store the decision per frame with p_add_proto_data() and set the flag
    only on the first pass.

    The TDS 4/5 login packet now changes the conversation encodings only
    on the first pass, and shows the int4 option with the int4 value.
    The capability length clamp was reversed and wrapped, and the
    capability loop did not count the length field itself. The param and
    row format token lengths are 2 bytes and now use the int2 encoding.
    A language token with length 0 no longer underflows. The nanoseconds
    of TIMEN, DATETIME2 and DATETIMEOFFSET were always 0 because of a cast
    placed before the multiplication, and TIMEN lengths above 5 are
    rejected. smalldatetime used a length of 8 for a 4 byte value, and
    the UDT assembly qualified name length no longer wraps in 16 bits. The
    TDS 4 and 5 protocol preferences left the date encodings of the
    conversation uninitialized.

