commit 37f6e9c8eb
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:29 2026 +1000

    TCPCL: Bound segments per transfer, fix session extension table

    The segment and ack lists of a transfer are searched linearly for every
    XFER_SEGMENT and XFER_ACK, and fragment_add_seq_next() walks the
    fragment list of the transfer on every segment. The transfer ID comes
    from the packet, so a capture with many small segments of one transfer
    makes the dissection quadratic (40000 segments of 18 bytes take 93
    seconds). Track at most 5000 segments and 5000 acks per transfer; a
    further segment is not analyzed or reassembled and gets an expert info.
    The sequence bookkeeping now also runs when the sequence analysis
    preference is off, so that the limit applies to reassembly alone.

    The SESS_INIT session extension items were looked up in the transfer
    extension table, so a session extension of type 1 was shown as the
    transfer extension "Transfer Length". Use the session extension table.

    The TCPCLv3 SHUTDOWN message advanced the offset by 1 after the 2 byte
    delay field; advance by 2.

