commit f1c80e078b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:20:28 2026 +1000

    SPDY: Keep decompressed headers per frame

    Every decompressed header block was appended to a file-scope list that
    was searched linearly, keyed only by stream ID and frame type, for every
    header frame. With many frames on different streams this took quadratic
    time (60000 frames took 46 s). The search also skipped the first list
    entry, so on a second pass the first header frame was decompressed again
    with an advanced zlib stream and failed, and blocks were shared between
    conversations that reuse stream IDs.

    Keep the list of decompressed blocks per frame with p_add_proto_data()
    instead, so a lookup only walks the blocks of the frame being dissected
    and later passes find what the first pass stored.

    Show the GOAWAY status with the GOAWAY status names and remove a stray
    closing parenthesis from its text.

