commit cb99473337
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 10:08:12 2026 -0500

    PROFINET: Key the per-AR station info by AR UUID in its own map

    The PNIO dissector stored and looked up the per-AR stationInfo in the
    conversation's proto_data using the AR UUID (its first 32-bit word, or a
    fixed "fake" AR UUID) as the key. conversation_add_proto_data() /
    conversation_get_proto_data() index that table by registered protocol
    id, so using an AR UUID there misuses the API and puts attacker-controlled
    packet data into the protocol-id keyspace.

    When the AR UUID word equals another dissector's runtime protocol id on
    the same conversation, the two dissectors exchange structures of
    different types: that dissector retrieves the PNIO stationInfo as its own
    type, and PNIO retrieves its structure as a stationInfo. With WCP, for
    example, a crafted AR UUID equal to proto_wcp makes wcp_uncompress()
    treat an 80-byte stationInfo as a wcp_circuit_data_t and follow an
    uninitialized buffer pointer, a null-pointer store that crashes TShark
    (packet-wcp.c) from packet data with default settings.

    Keep the per-AR stationInfo in a per-conversation wmem_map keyed by AR
