commit 1b50cb227c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:01 2026 +1000

    RTSP: Fix abort on dest_addr without closing quote

    In rtsp_create_conversation(), sscanf() of "\"%u.%u.%u.%u\"" returns 4
    even when the closing quote is missing, so strstr() returned NULL and
    g_strndup(tmp, tmp2 - tmp) asked for about 2^64 bytes, which makes GLib
    abort. Check the result of strstr() for the closing quote, and for the
    ':' in the two other address forms, and report a bad address instead.

    dest_addr and src_addr were both stored through the same ip4_addr
    variable, and set_address() only keeps a pointer, so the destination
    address silently became the source address when both were present. Use
    separate variables.

    A Content-Type header with an empty media type made the parameter end
    offset smaller than the value offset, so the length wrapped and the
    frame was shown as malformed. Use a length of zero in that case.

