commit 3220351d6d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 05:03:01 2026 +1000

    RTPS: Bound TypeObject and typecode dissection, fix stack pointers

    A TypeObject received in discovery could make dissect_user_defined()
    run for hours: the members of a structure beyond the display limit are
    still walked, so a chain of structures costs N^D calls. The preference
    that enables user data dissection is bypassed because a custom type with
    the id of a builtin type (for example InstanceStateDataResponse) was
    found before the builtin one. Look up the builtin types first, and stop
    a sample after 50000 dissect_user_defined() calls with the existing
    user data dissection error.

    rtps_util_add_typecode() recursed through TK_SEQUENCE without counting
    the nesting, so a large reassembled PID_TYPECODE overflowed the stack.
    Count the nesting for sequences, and stop with a new expert info when
    the dissection depth gets close to the maximum tree depth, before the
    depth assertion fires.

    Members of a typecode struct or union could overlap, all pointing at
    the same nested typecode, which made the work and the memory grow
    exponentially. Stop when a member starts before the end of the nested
    typecode of the previous one. The indent string is now allocated from
    the packet pool instead of the epan scope, where it was never freed.

    dissection_info was allocated without zeroing, so an array with an empty
    bound sequence used an uninitialized bound. Use wmem_new0().

    The RTPS_ROOT_MESSAGE_KEY and RTPS_CURRENT_SUBMESSAGE_COL_DATA_KEY
    proto data pointed at locals of dissect_rtps() and
    dissect_rtps_submessages(), which RTPS-PROC used after they returned.
    Allocate both from the packet pool.

    Only fill the TypeObject maps on the first pass, so that redissection
    gives the same result. PID_EXTENDED is now compared for equality instead
    of as a mask.

    rtps_util_add_type_id_v2() recurses for the element type of plain
    sequence, array and map type identifiers without a bound. Without a
    tree a chain of nested sequence identifiers in a reassembled
    PID_TYPE_INFORMATION overflowed the stack. Count it with
    increment_dissection_depth() and stop with a new expert info before
    the depth limit, as the typecode code does.

    rtps_util_look_for_secure_tag() advanced by the submessage length
    without the 4 octet header and subtracted the length twice, so a zero
    length submessage after a protected body looped forever when PSK
    decryption was enabled. Skip the header and the body.

    The type mapping kept for a discovered endpoint was allocated with
    wmem_new() and only fields_visited and the GUID flags were cleared, so
    a DATA_BATCH of an endpoint whose discovery data had no type id looked
    up an uninitialized type id (valgrind). Allocate it with wmem_new0().

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
