commit 6246b60295
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RELOAD: Fix an infinite loop and CPU blow-ups on malformed messages

    A message extension with a content length of 0xfffffff9 made the
    truncation check wrap to zero and the loop advance by zero, so the
    dissector never returned. Compare the length against the remaining
    extension bytes without overflow. The MessageContents length check is
    done in 64 bits as well, and before the extensions length is read.

    In StoredDataSpecifier the dictionary key loop always read from the
    start of the specifier instead of the key list, and the keys length was
    not checked against the specifier length, giving tens of millions of
    iterations per packet. Read from the current key and limit the keys
    length to the specifier's length field.

    dissect_diagnosticinfo() returned 2 + length instead of 4 + length and
    walked the length of the whole remaining list instead of its own, which
    was quadratic. Return 4 + length and bound the info by its own length.

    Also fix small errors: the hop counter in a DiagnosticResponse was not
    skipped, and the list subtree hung off the wrong item; the IPv6
    IpAddressPort item was 6 bytes long instead of 18; the ArrayRange item
    was 16 bytes instead of 8; the ICE candidate priority offset missed the
    candidate offset; the error code was read at the forwarding header
    length instead of the current offset (wrong after reassembly); the
    truncated FindKindData and SipRegistration data items were at the wrong
