commit e3be3e4a4f
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RTCP: Bound transport-cc allocations and fix several decoding bugs

    The transport-cc feedback dissector allocated two zeroed arrays sized
    from the packet status count (up to 65535 entries) for every FCI,
    before validating anything. A 64 KB packet holding thousands of tiny
    FCIs, each failing the run length check and returning early, allocated
    about 1.3 GB from the packet pool. Allocate the two arrays once per
    RTCP packet with a fixed size of 65536 entries and only read back the
    entries that were filled in (delta_index), so no per-FCI zeroing is
    needed.

    Fix the XR IDMS block, which did not advance past the NTP receive
    timestamp (so the RTP timestamp overlapped it and the next block was
    decoded four bytes early) and which decoded the timestamp as raw
    seconds/nanoseconds instead of NTP.

    Fix the REMB loop, which assigned instead of accumulated the number of
    FCI entries read, so a second REMB block ran past the packet. Fix the
    MS dominant speaker history, which counted bytes in steps of two while
    each entry is four bytes. Fix an unsigned comparison that was always
    true for the trailing PSFB FCI, clamp the profile specific extension
    bytes consumed to the remaining length, and do not subtract an RTCP
    padding count that is larger than the packet.

    Use the floor revoke cause strings for floor revoke in the Info column,
    use the whole setup_method buffer when copying the setup method, and
    make the transport-cc receive delta padding field FT_BYTES so any
    padding length is valid.

    The TMMBR/TMMBN measured overhead (the low 9 bits of the last two
    octets of the FCI) was read from the last octet onwards, one octet past
    the FCI, so a packet ending with such an FCI was malformed.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 62ce1fd99059bf5f6c24f4de25360401dba454c2)
    [Backport: kept this branch's int offset and packet_len in
    dissect_rtcp_rtpfb_transport_cc_fci() and its caller while passing in
    the arrays allocated once per packet; dropped the padding count clamp,
    since this branch does not subtract the padding from the packet length;
    kept this branch's one-octet TMMBR measured overhead item, which does
    not read past the FCI; otherwise identical.]

commit d1cac33349
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RTLS: Bound the nesting of compound messages

    An AR_COMPOUND_MESSAGE_REPORT can contain further compound message
