commit 4bd978b142
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:01 2026 +1000

    RTITCP: Fix a message length wrap that loops forever

    dissect_control_message() returned uint16_t, so a control message with
    a length of 0xfff0 and the 16 octet CRC header returned 0x10000 as 0.
    The caller then never advanced its offset and looped forever, creating
    file scope allocations on every iteration for request messages until
    memory ran out. Return and keep the length as unsigned, and stop the
    loop if a message makes no progress.

    Do not add the error code description when the attribute is shorter
    than 4 octets (the length wrapped to a huge value). Add the port
    attribute with length 4 and the connection type attribute with length
    1, instead of the attribute length, which raised an expert info for the
    fixed size fields.

