commit 0a8de984a5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:00 2026 +1000

    EGFX: Fix endless loop on bad pduLength and partial ZGFX output

    A pduLength that points past the end of the data (for example
    0xFFFFFFF0) made nextOffset wrap back to the start, so the dissector
    looped forever when no tree was being built. nextOffset is now
    unsigned and a pduLength larger than the remaining data ends the
    dissection with an expert info.

    rdp8_decompress() (epan/tvbuff_rdp.c) allocated the multipart output
    from the size in the packet without zeroing it and returned it even
    when the segments filled only part of it, exposing uninitialized heap
    data. It now fails unless the segments produce exactly the announced
    size, and the announced size is bounded by segment_count times the
    64 KiB maximum output of one segment, which also limits the allocation
    that was up to 4 GiB.

    rdp8_decompress() returned the input tvb itself for a descriptor other
    than the two ZGFX ones. EGFX stored the returned tvb in a file-scope
    tree and used it again on later passes, after the packet's tvb had been
    freed (use after free with tshark -2 or in the GUI). The decompressed
    tvbs were also never freed. rdp8_decompress() now returns NULL for an
    unknown descriptor, the result is chained to the packet's tvb, and EGFX
    keeps the decompressed bytes (already file scope) for later passes and
    makes a child tvb from them on each pass.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 81dcd586e595a645450f68be3575ec5d186fa5b7)
    [Backport: this branch's tvbuff_rdp.h has no doc comment for
    rdp8_decompress(), so master's comment update was dropped;; cast
    tvb_reported_length_remaining() to uint32_t in the new pduLength
    comparison, as it returns int on this branch; otherwise identical.]

commit 278f58f63b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:26:00 2026 +1000

    DRDYNVC: Fix uninitialized PDU info, NULL channel and huge allocation

    The per-PDU info structure was allocated without zeroing and inserted
    in the PDU tree before it was filled. A middle fragment of a
    reassembly, or a payload larger than the pending length, left the tvb
    pointer uninitialized and it was later used as a tvbuff (wild pointer
    dereference). Both allocations are now zeroed and the entry is only
    inserted once the PDU is accepted.

    A Create Request seen before the UDP transport is linked to the main
    conversation creates no channel on the first pass; on later passes the
    channel stays NULL and was dereferenced. It is now checked.

    The reassembly buffer was preallocated with the announced PDU length,
    up to 4 GiB; it now grows with the data. A first chunk larger than the
    announced length no longer underflows pendingLen and is treated as a
    single packet. When ZGFX decompression fails the raw data is used
    instead of a NULL tvb.

    Reassembled and decompressed payloads were kept as tvbs across passes
    and never freed; keep their (file scope) data instead, chain the
    decompressed tvb to the packet's tvb, and make a child tvb on each pass.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit c4b92f84b454d99af6e4d1670282b63c64b9c627)
