commit 4b26df0aeb
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 18:54:24 2026 +1000

    NVMe: Use one key shape for data_responses and fix small decode bugs

    nvme_add_data_tr_pkt() and nvme_lookup_data_tr_pkt() built the key as
    [frame] when the rkey (the command ID for NVMe/TCP) was 0 and as
    [cid][frame] otherwise, in the same wmem tree. A C2HData PDU with
    command ID 0 in frame N stored a command context at the first level
    for key N, and a later PDU with command ID N then descended into it
    as if it were a subtree, crashing in wmem_alloc(). Always use the two
    level key [rkey][frame]. NVMe/RDMA passes an rkey of 0 and so keeps a
    consistent key shape.

    Also fix three small problems. The Self-test log page decoder never
    incremented the result index, so every entry was labelled "latest 0".
    add_ctrl_rab() and add_ctrl_mdts() shifted by a raw byte value, which
    is undefined for values of 64 or more; they now print "overflow". The
    Get Log Page NUMD byte count was computed with the +1 done in 32 bits;
    do it in 64 bits.

