commit 8e325922bf
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 21:00:00 2026 +1000

    MsgPack: Fix endless loop and unbounded recursion

    An unsupported type byte (0xC1) did not advance the offset. Inside an
    array or map with a 32-bit element count this looped up to 4 billion
    times, adding an expert info and a column string each time, until memory
    ran out. Consume the type byte after reporting it.

    Nested arrays and maps recursed without any limit, one byte per level,
    and overflowed the stack. Limit the nesting to 32 levels, tracked per
    packet with p_get_proto_depth(), and report "Nesting too deep" with a
    new expert info msgpack.too_deep.

    Also fix the "float 64" typo and give the negative fixint field its own
    filter name, msgpack.integer.negfixint, instead of registering
    msgpack.integer.fixint twice.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit a904409dcd501c984bd64c747626dc936413f65f)
    [Backport: this branch only decodes fixmap and fixarray (at most 15
    elements), so an unsupported type cannot loop billions of times here,
    but nested arrays and maps still recurse one byte per level. The patch
    was rewritten for this branch's older code: the 32 level nesting limit
    with msgpack.too_deep, and consuming the unsupported type byte. The
    float 64 and negfixint field changes do not apply.]

commit be154ec754
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 19:03:59 2026 +1000

    MCPE: Bound Batch nesting and drop an assertion

    A Batch packet can contain another Batch, and each level decompresses
    its payload and recurses. Only the tree depth limit stopped this, and
    only when a tree was built. Allow at most 16 nested Batches per packet,
    stop with an expert info (mcpe.batch.too_deep) beyond that, and wrap
    the nested dissector call with increment_dissection_depth() and
    decrement_dissection_depth().

    Replace DISSECTOR_ASSERT(message_id == 0xFE) in the heuristic
    dissector with a plain check, and use uint8_t for the packet id in
    test_mcpe_heur() so that ids above 0x7f are not sign-extended.

