commit 2cda55bb4b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 12:37:10 2026 +1000

    IPMI: Bound nesting, FRU Unicode length and request list

    Nested Send Message / Get Message commands called back into
    dissect_ipmi_cmd() without any limit, so a packet with many nested
    levels overflowed the stack when ipmi.dissect_bus_commands is enabled.
    The uint8_t level counters also wrapped at 256. Stop at 32 levels (or
    when the layer count approaches the tree depth limit) with a new expert
    info, and wrap the command handler call in
    increment/decrement_dissection_depth().

    For FRU Unicode strings with an odd byte length, the character buffer
    was sized at 3 * len + 1 but parse_unicode() wrote 6 characters for
    each 2-byte pair, including a trailing partial pair, overflowing the
    heap buffer and reading past the string. Size it as (len / 2) * 6 so
    only whole pairs are decoded.

    The per-conversation list of unmatched requests grew without bound and
    was scanned linearly for every response, which is quadratic for
    captures whose requests share a timestamp. Keep at most 1024 entries
    and drop the oldest.

    Also fix two small decoding errors: the offset after the full 6-bit
    ASCII triplets was advanced by len / 4 instead of (len / 4) * 3, and
    the Type/Length Type item was given the shifted type instead of the
    type/length byte, so it always showed 0 with its 0xc0 mask.

