commit d30029ef07
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 21:56:17 2026 -0500

    Diameter: Bound grouped AVP recursion and fix several decoding issues

    Grouped AVPs were dissected recursively without any bound, so a message
    with deeply nested grouped AVPs over the default TCP/SCTP port 3868
    overflowed the stack, also without a tree. Track the nesting with
    increment_dissection_depth()/decrement_dissection_depth().

    diam_sub_dis_t.item was only set by unsigned32_avp() and never reset,
    so an AVP subdissector that hides "the item created in
    packet-diameter.c" could hide the value of an earlier, unrelated AVP.
    Reset it before each AVP is dissected and after a grouped AVP, and set
    it in unsigned64_avp() as well.

    With the session_imsi preference enabled the Session-Id to IMSI map was
    updated and consulted on every pass, so "Associated IMSI" depended on
    the dissection order and tshark -2 differed from one pass. Update the
    map on the first pass only and keep the result per PDU with
    p_add_proto_data().

    Smaller fixes:
    - CC-Total-Octets printed a uint64_t with %d and claimed 16 bytes; use
      PRIu64 and return 8. Mark add_group_str() with G_GNUC_PRINTF and use
      %u for the unsigned Result-Code and Rating-Group values.
    - Framed-IPv6-Prefix masked the byte after the prefix, with the wrong
      bits, instead of the last partial prefix byte.
    - The dictionary "value=" processing instruction skipped only
      strlen("key=\"") characters, so the parsed value was always "=".
      Skip strlen("value=\"").
    - dissect_diameter_avps() did not default Subscription-Id-Type and
      User-Equipment-Info-Type to unknown, so they were treated as E.164
      and IMEISV.
    - 3GPP Path used the absolute comma offset as the item length, so the
      second and later entries were too long and the last one was lost.
    - 3GPP QoS transfer delay compared the whole octet instead of the
      6-bit value, giving nonsense delays.
    - SM-RP-UI did not restore the column writability or p2p_dir when GSM
      SMS threw an exception, and never restored p2p_dir at all; use
      TRY/FINALLY.

    The spare bits of DER-S6b-Flags (3GPP AVP 1523) were registered with a
    bitmask of 0 although they are in the bitmask array given to
    proto_tree_add_bitmask_with_flags(), so every S6b DER with that AVP
    failed DISSECTOR_ASSERT(hf->bitmask != 0) when dissected with a tree.
    Give them the mask 0xFFFFFFFE, as the other flag AVPs with one defined
    bit have.

    The map from command name to SRT row index was one global shared by
    every Diameter SRT table, and each table's init function replaced it.
    With two tables (two -z diameter,srt options or two Service Response
    Time dialogs) a row index created by one table was used by the other,
    which never created that row, and add_srt_table_data() wrote past the
    end of its procedures array. Look the command up in the rows of the
    table being updated instead.

    grouped_avp() cleared the grouped state (dis_gouped, group_avp_code and
    the Vendor-Id) when a nested grouped AVP ended, so the AVPs after it in
    the enclosing group were treated as top level: a Result-Code after the
    Granted-Service-Unit of a Multiple-Services-Credit-Control became
    Result-Code-Command-Level and was missing from the MSCC text. Restore
    the state of the enclosing group instead. Also undo the dissection
    depth (and the group state) when an exception leaves a grouped AVP, so
    that the next PDU of the same TCP segment does not start with a higher
    depth.

    In the "diameter_avps" dissector an EAP-Message AVP let EAP replace the
    "AVPs:" list in the Info column. Put the list back after the AVPs.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit 48a21dcb7220557599f63c4e91b0c171f7e870bf)

    Co-authored-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit cf1ef40389e49ed5151146354b943dd99eb4374b)

    Backport: Keep the older grouped-AVP tree and IMSI helper APIs; omit absent group summary strings and adapt comma scanning.

