commit 13b6d2028e
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 19:03:59 2026 +1000

    Modbus: Fix quadratic request matching and short PDU handling

    Every Modbus query was prepended to a per-conversation list that was
    never trimmed, and every response walked that list looking for a
    matching function code, transaction id and unit id. A capture with many
    queries and many (unmatched) responses took O(queries x responses)
    time, 38 seconds for a 668 KB file. Replace the list with a wmem_map
    keyed on transaction id, unit id and function code that holds the most
    recent request. The matching result is unchanged: the most recent
    earlier request with the same key. The match is made on the first pass
    only and stored per frame as before.

    classify_mbrtu_packet() and dissect_mbrtu_pdu_common() kept the length
    in an uint8_t/uint16_t, which truncates for large PDUs. Use unsigned,
    and return early from the RTU dissector when fewer than 4 bytes are
    present, so that len - 2 and len - 3 cannot go negative. Return from
    dissect_mbtcp_pdu_common() after the invalid length expert info when
    the length field is below 2 instead of creating a zero-length subset.

    The modbus_conversation structure in packet-mbtcp.h changes from a
    list to a map.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
