commit f008e07bdf
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 15:16:33 2026 +1000

    PIM: Bound Register nesting and fix several decoding errors

    A Register message carries an IP packet, which can itself carry a PIM
    Register, so a packet could nest IP and PIM hundreds of levels deep
    until the generic layer limit assertion fired. Both the PIM v2 and v1
    Register dissection now allow at most 4 nested Register messages per
    packet, track the nesting with p_get_proto_depth(), wrap the nested
    call in increment/decrement_dissection_depth() and add an expert info
    (pim.nesting_too_deep) beyond the limit.

    The DF-Election subtype was read from the first byte of the message
    instead of the high nibble of the second one, so the Backoff and Pass
    bodies were never dissected. The Join Attribute RLOC address family was
    read at the address offset instead of the attribute offset, the RLOC
    item showed the outer address instead of the RLOC, and the IPv6 text
    used the IPv4 formatter.

