commit b4a3748593
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 12:30:39 2026 +1000

    LBMR: Fix TNWG option loop and swapped LBTRDMA arguments

    dissect_lbmr_tnwg_opts() added each option length to a running total
    and then subtracted that total from the remaining length and added it
    to the offset on every pass, so offsets were wrong from the second
    option on. The context instance, address and domain handlers also
    return their own length byte, which can be 0, so a zero-length option
    never advanced the loop and hung the dissector. Use the length of each
    option, and add an expert info and stop when the length byte is shorter
    than the option header.

    The TNWG interest records had the same problem: a record length of 0
    kept the record loop at one offset for up to 65535 records, which ends
    in the too-many-items error. Stop with an expert info when a record is
    shorter than its header.

    In the TIR LBTRDMA case, lbtrdma_transport_add() and
    lbtrdma_transport_source_string() take (address, session_id, port) but
    were called with port and session_id swapped. Pass them in the right
    order.

