commit f94536b08c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 19:55:21 2026 +1000

    IuUP: Fix an out-of-bounds read, an assertion and a loop

    The heuristic dissector passed a byte from the packet as the length of
    the two-octet array given to crc6_0X6F(), reading far beyond the stack
    array. It also read the header without checking that three bytes are
    available. Pass the constant length 2, which matches the header CRC
    computed by add_hdr_crc(), and reject packets shorter than 3 bytes.

    dissect_rfcis() used DISSECTOR_ASSERT(c < 64) on the number of RFCI
    records, which a packet can exceed. Report it with an expert info and
    stop. dissect_iuup_payload() did not advance when the RFCI had no
    subflows or all lengths were zero, looping forever; break out when no
    bits were consumed.

    The heuristic CRC10 check for data PDUs with CRC used offset 4 instead
    of 2 as add_payload_crc() does, reading two bytes past the end of the
    packet. Use offset 2.

