commit d583c77f5d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 06:45:19 2026 +1000

    HTTP: Do not assert in streaming mode or on repeated CONNECT tunnels

    A Content-Length header in a message that is being dissected in
    streaming chunk mode (Transfer-Encoding: chunked with a streaming
    content type such as application/grpc-web, or pipelined messages that
    pick up the streaming state of another message) hit a
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT_HINT(). Add the "Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding
    set together" expert info and ignore the Content-Length instead, as
    Transfer-Encoding overrides it (RFC 9112 section 6.3).

    The assertions in dissect_http_on_stream() that the headers exist on a
    later pass and that all streaming state exists when a new streaming
    reassembly is started can be reached by pipelined messages too. Dissect
    the message without streaming mode when that state is missing instead
    of asserting.

    The http_seq statistics created a child node when the referer was the
    request URI itself, and walked the whole parent chain for every packet,
    which was quadratic for long referer chains. Do not create such a node
    and limit the walk to 64 levels.

    Two CONNECT requests to the same target, both answered, made the
    tunnelled data recurse through HTTP until the layer depth assertion in
    packet.c fired. Count the tunnel nesting with
    increment_dissection_depth() and pass the data to the data dissector
    with an expert info before the layer limit is reached.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
