commit 2c803c7cff
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 10:18:28 2026 +1000

    BEEP: Loop over the messages in a frame, step over the previous payload

    Messages after the first one in a frame were dissected by a recursive
    call for each, so a frame of 500 or more messages (17 KB on TCP 10288)
    failed the DISSECTOR_ASSERT() in increment_dissection_depth(). Loop
    over the messages in dissect_beep() instead.

    When a frame continued the payload of the previous frame's message,
    the first pass created the per-frame data with the bytes left but did
    not step over them, so the frame was parsed from its first octet; the
    later passes did step over them, and tshark -2 gave different output.
    Create the per-frame data first and then always step over what is
    left, and add that payload to the BEEP tree instead of the top level.

