commit 5679cee490
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 17:44:58 2026 +1000

    ANSI MAP: Dissect the SMS bearer data only once

    The SMS bearer data was kept after it had been handed to the IS-637,
    IS-683 or IS-801 dissector, and every following TeleserviceIdentifier
    or ServiceIndicator parameter handed it over again. The BER SET decoder
    accepts repeated members, so a message with a few hundred of them added
    a layer each time until the layer limit in call_dissector_work() failed
    its DISSECTOR_ASSERT(). Forget the bearer data once it is dissected.

    A ReturnResult whose invoke ANSI MAP had not saved, for example because
    the invoke was malformed, was dissected with the operation code of the
    last packet dissected, so its decoding depended on the order packets
    were viewed in. Use the operation code TCAP matched instead. That is
    also used without a transaction ID, which was passed to snprintf() as
    a NULL string.

    Also show the matched operation for ReturnError and Reject in the Info
    column, and keep counting known operations in the statistics after an
    unknown one; a static flag stopped that for the rest of the session.

    Every MSLocation parameter was malformed, because the 1 or 2 octet
    resolution was added to an 8-bit field with length -1, and a 1-octet
    SMS-TeleserviceIdentifier threw, because it was read from the enclosing
    tvb.

