commit d84ad158c8
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 15:16:33 2026 +1000

    PLDM: Fix a leak and 16-bit offset wrap

    The type map for GetPLDMCommands was created with wmem_map_new() in a
    NULL allocator scope for every request, so each request leaked a map,
    and the map held only the last request, rewritten on every pass. Create
    one autoreset map in proto_register_pldm(), insert into it only on the
    first pass, and remember the type looked up by a response with
    p_add_proto_data() so later passes decode it the same way.

    parse_fru_record_table(), dissect_FRU() and dissect_FWU() kept the
    offset in a uint16_t. For a PDU longer than 65535 bytes the offset
    wrapped and the FRU table loop reread the same bytes until the tree
    item limit stopped it. Use unsigned offsets.

    Compute the padding before the FRU table CRC as unsigned and only add
    the CRC when at least 4 bytes remain, and print a non-printable alpha
    version byte as '?'.

    dissect_pldm() did nothing without a tree, so on a first pass without
    one (tshark -2, the GUI) the request map stayed empty and responses lost
    their type. Dissect without a tree too.

