commit 2a2a4d9a8f
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 12:57:20 2026 +1000

    NFS: Fix a CPU blow-up and bad lengths in the SCSI layout and snooping

    dissect_nfs4_vol_indices() added the same 4-byte item num_vols times
    without advancing the offset. With a count of 0xffffffff and in-bounds
    bytes no exception stopped the loop, so one GETDEVICEINFO reply took
    tens of seconds. Advance the offset by 4 for each index.

    With file name snooping enabled, a file handle length of 0x80000000 or
    more became negative and reached tvb_memdup(), which asserts. Reject a
    file handle length that is zero, negative or larger than 128 at the top
    of the three snooping helpers. Skip empty names when snooping READDIRPLUS
    entries, and make nfs_full_name_snoop() check name_len and the start of
    the buffer before reading the character before them, which was a one
    byte heap read before the buffer.

    Decode the SCSI SLICE and STRIPE volumes at the right offsets: start
    and length are 8 bytes and the stripe unit is 8 bytes (RFC 8154), so
    make those three fields FT_UINT64 and advance past them.

    Use the "unknown" permission tables in dissect_nfs4_acemask() for an
    object type that is neither a file nor a directory, so NULL is never
    passed to "%s".

    The snooping hash tables for READDIR parents and unmatched names never
    freed their keys, which leaked 8 bytes per call; free them with the
    table. Free the previous full name when a file handle is matched again
    instead of leaking it.

    Assisted-by: Claude
