commit 184e0db51f
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 16:22:14 2026 +1000

    ETW: Bound the formatted message size

    format_message() replaced every "%N" in the event message with the
    value of property N, with no limit on the size of the result. A record
    of a few hundred kilobytes could make the output several gigabytes and
    abort the process. The formatted output is now capped at 64 KiB; once
    the next substitution would exceed it, the rest of the message is
    appended unformatted.

    startLoc was a uint16_t and wrapped for messages longer than 65535
    characters, restarting later appends at the wrong place. Make it
    unsigned.

    Pass NULL instead of the frame's pseudo header to mbim.control, which
    casts its data to urb_info_t, and a zeroed struct tcpinfo to nbss,
    which expects one, rather than relying on the pseudo header happening
    to be all zeros.

    Do not add the PROV_TRAITS provider name when the traits size is less
    than 2, which gave a length of -2 or -1.

    The FILETIME to Unix time conversion used an unsigned subtraction, so
    timestamps before 1970 wrapped to a far future time. Use a signed value
    and normalize the nanoseconds so they are never negative.

    The source and destination addresses, the provider name and the message
    come from pinfo->pool, but were set with col_set_str(), which keeps the
    pointer and requires a string that outlives the packet. Use
    col_add_str() so the text is copied.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

