commit cbd716633a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 10:35:11 2026 +1000

    BVLC: Dissect the secured message of a Secure-BVLL, not the BVLL again

    For an unencrypted Secure-BVLL the dissector called itself on the same
    tvb from offset 0, which read the same Secure-BVLL header again. The
    only thing that changed per level was the 16-octet signature the
    security wrapper cut off the end, so a datagram of about 8 KB nested
    500 levels deep and failed the dissection depth assertion, on the
    default port. Dissect the data after the security wrapper instead, and
    do not decode a Secure-BVLL inside a Secure-BVLL.

    The security wrapper shortens the tvb to the secured data, and for an
    encrypted Secure-BVLL the dissector returned the shortened length, 0,
    so UDP tried BVLC again and the packet was malformed. Return the length
    from before the wrapper.

