commit afe5ee2e23
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 15:16:33 2026 +1000

    PKCS12: Fix stale pointers kept across packets and ber.oid handling

    The object identifier string is kept in a file scope pointer into the
    packet pool and was never reset, so a SafeBag, CertBag, CRLBag,
    SecretBag or PKCS12Attribute without its identifier passed the string
    of an earlier, freed packet to call_ber_oid_callback(), a heap
    use-after-free. Reset it at the start of each of these sequences.

    The salt tvbuff and iteration count used for decryption were likewise
    left over from an earlier packet when a PBE algorithm had no
    parameters, and generate_key_or_iv() used the freed tvbuff. Record per
    packet, with p_add_proto_data(), that parameters were parsed, and treat
    them as missing otherwise. The key derivation itself is unchanged.

    The PFX and AuthenticatedSafe dissectors changed the ber.oid entry for
    id-data and restored it only on normal return, so an exception left
    later CMS data being dissected as PKCS#12, and each call created a new
    dissector handle. Create the two handles once in handoff, and restore
    the previous handle in a cleanup function that also runs on exceptions,
    which also makes nesting restore correctly.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

