commit da49a80ac2
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 19:55:21 2026 +1000

    ISUP: Fix range and status assert and several field decoding errors

    The Range and status parameter computed the range as a uint8_t octet
    plus one, which wraps to 0 for an octet of 0xFF. The following
    proto_tree_add_uint_bits_format_value() call with 0 bits then reached
    REPORT_DISSECTOR_BUG. Compute the range as an unsigned value so the
    1..8 bit branch is never entered with a zero width.

    Reset the file-scope called number and cause value together with the
    calling number at the start of each message, so stale values from a
    previous packet are not reported to the tap.

    Fix the 2-octet CODEC list length in the BAT ASE dissection to combine
    the octets the same way the outer loop does, the 2-octet application
