commit 64f7d1a6b0
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 06:45:20 2026 +1000

    IEEE1905: Fix MIC check buffer overflow and small length bugs

    check_mic_tlv() allocated DECRYPT_MIC_CMDU_OCTETS + tlvs_len bytes but
    copied the 6 CMDU bytes, the 13 MIC TLV header bytes and all TLVs other
    than the MIC TLV into it, so a short MIC TLV overflowed the heap buffer.
    Size the buffer for everything written, check every copy against the
    remaining TLV data and the allocation, and use unsigned lengths. Reject
    a MIC TLV that is shorter than its fixed part plus the MIC with an
    expert info before the check is attempted.

    dissect_qos_management_descriptor() subtracted 14 from an unsigned
    16-bit length without checking it, and could loop forever on a
    zero-sized or oversized tagged field. Check the length and stop.

    Also fix the version extraction in check_mic_tlv(), where & bound
    tighter than the shift, and ieee1905_fragment_equal(), which compared the
    source address twice instead of source and destination, and the push
    button join notification TLV, which added its two MAC addresses with a
    length of 2 so that the TLV was always malformed.

    Assisted-by: Claude
