commit 8a2076d8e0
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 17:39:52 2026 +1000

    H.223: Fix mux sublist size and avoid an assertion and endless loop

    mux_element_sublist_size() started at the second element of the list
    it was given, so a sublist consisting of a single element (for example
    one with untilClosingFlag, stored as a repeat count of 0) got size 0.
    That tripped DISSECTOR_ASSERT(length != 0), reachable with a crafted
    H.245 MultiplexEntrySend, and would have made the caller's loop run
    forever. The sum was also a uint32_t that could wrap with nested
    repeat counts.

    Start at the first element, sum in 64 bits and clamp, and return 0
    instead of asserting. The caller reports an expert info and stops when
    the sublist size is 0, and compares against the remaining length
    without overflow.

    Also make h223.mux.mpl an FT_UINT8 without the stale 0xf00f mask, hold
    the payload length in a uint32_t, allocate the mux table item only
    after the early returns in add_h223_mux_element() so that it is not
    leaked, and drop a duplicated include.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 87dabea9c3552ec4bdbec18c93f05cf234b39b47)

