commit e0a4b964f5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 16:52:54 2026 +1000

    EHDLC: Stop on a DataLen shorter than the header

    A TFP or P-GSL frame (SAPI 10, 11 or 12) with a DataLen of 0 never
    advanced the offset, because the "len == 0" guard at the end of the
    loop was skipped by the "continue". The same header was dissected
    again and again, each time calling the subdissector, until the layer
    depth DISSECTOR_ASSERT in epan/packet.c fired. With a DataLen of 0 or
    1, "len - 2" also passed a wrapped length to the subset tvb, and the
    same underflow could happen with "len - header_length" for the other
    frames.

    Add an expert info and stop dissecting when DataLen is shorter than
    the address and length fields, and again when it is shorter than the
    header including the control field. This replaces the old "len == 0"
    guard.

    dissect_ehdlc_xid() parsed IEs up to the end of the tvb, not the end
    of the frame, so it took any following frames as XID IEs. Bound the
    loop with the frame length.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
