commit 22c04aaa93
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 02:52:56 2026 +1000

    CMS: Stop nested content before the layer limit, keep digests apart

    The content of a ContentInfo, and the eContent of an
    EncapsulatedContentInfo, are dissected through the BER OID table, which
    can lead back to ContentInfo. Each level adds a layer, so a message
    nested about 600 times deep hit the DISSECTOR_ASSERT on the number of
    layers in call_dissector_work(). Stop with an expert info before the
    limit, as ASAM CMP does.

    The content that a messageDigest attribute is checked against was kept
    for the whole packet. A detached SignedData after another ContentInfo
    in the same packet had its digest checked against the content of the
    earlier message, and could show it as correct. Give each ContentInfo
    its own content.

    id-aes256-CCM was registered under 2.16.840.1.101.3.4.1.44, the OID of
    id-aes256-CFB. It is 2.16.840.1.101.3.4.1.47.

