commit 56b4fb2d2f
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 19:30:49 2026 +1000

    ANSI TCAP: Stop handing components over before the layer limit

    Each component of a package was handed to ANSI MAP, AIN or the national
    opcode dissector, and each hand-off added a protocol layer to the
    frame. A package with about 500 components reached the layer limit in
    call_dissector_work() and failed its DISSECTOR_ASSERT(), losing the
    rest of the frame. Stop handing components over when the frame is
    close to the limit, and report it with an expert info instead.

    A result was matched with the last invoke saved for its transaction up
    to and including its own frame. In the first pass only the invokes
    before it in the frame were saved, in later passes all of them, so a
    package with an invoke after the result decoded differently with
    tshark -2. Match only invokes of earlier frames.

    Also keep the whole length of a transaction ID longer than 255 octets;
    it was truncated to 8 bits.

