commit d300abcf5b
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 15:16:33 2026 +1000

    PPCAP: Use NUL terminated copies for string addresses

    The Node Id source and destination addresses were created with
    set_address_tvb(AT_STRINGZ) directly on packet bytes. A zero length
    gave NULL address data, which g_strlcpy() rejects, and a string without
    a NUL made the address code read past the field. Use a NUL terminated
    copy in the packet pool and skip the address when the length is 0.

