commit 3222818243
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 15:16:33 2026 +1000

    P_MUL: Do not assert on a relative message ID seen on a later pass

    message_id_offset used 0 both for "not set yet" and for "set to 0".
    When the first PDU had message ID 0 and a later one a different ID, the
    offset changed between the first and the second pass, the first PDU then
    got a bogus relative ID, register_p_mul_id() found no entry for it and
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT(pkg_data) fired.

    Track whether the offset is set with a separate flag, reset by the init
    routine and set only once (both for the message ID and the Ack loop),
    and return NULL instead of asserting when no saved data exists; the
    callers already handle NULL.

