    of length - 4; the Prefix-Elision option never advanced its offset and
    read the prefix one byte too far; the BCP MAC L and M bit masks pointed
    at the wrong byte; capture_ppp_hdlc tested pd[0] instead of pd[offset];
    the PPPMux flags were added to the top-level tree instead of the header
    subtree; and the LCP variable-length option error always named the
    Vendor option and "6" bytes instead of the actual option and length.

