    bytes for an assignment. A 1.3 KB packet ran about 16 million loop
    iterations, 0.35 s per packet without a tree, and with a tree it hit
    the "possible infinite loop" check. Add an expert info for an unknown
    assignment format and stop dissecting the table there, because the
    size of an assignment entry is not known.

    The Network Layer Info descriptor passed the literal 1 to
    dissect_snmp_pdu() as the protocol id, which is the "Wireshark
    Columns" protocol. The SNMP PDU was shown under a "Wireshark Columns"
    item and the Protocol column was set to "Columns". Look up the SNMP
    protocol id in the handoff and pass that.

    The Route id loop count field had the mask 0x01 of the Route id flag
    field before it, so at most 2 route ids were read. Remove the mask, as
    for the other loop count fields of the descriptor.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit e3363ed1640ae429da40dcd048803cad56d438b1)

    Backport: Retain the separate assignment-format read used on release-5.0.

    Assisted-by: Codex

    (cherry picked from commit fcdde2569ebd3bcaf77ac4ab134296530d9071ff)

