commit 5247d6d5e3
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 18:54:24 2026 +1000

    OpenFlow: Fix endless loops and unbounded recursion in v4, v5 and v6

    The v5 and v6 property, instruction and match helpers handled a too
    short element length with "offset = length", where length is the
    length of the message. For a message nested in another one (the data of
    OFPT_ERROR, OFPT_REQUESTFORWARD, OFPT_BUNDLE_ADD_MESSAGE) the nested
    message was dissected on the outer tvb at an absolute offset with the
    relative inner length, so this moved the offset backwards and the
    callers, which loop on the absolute element end, parsed the same
    elements forever while adding expert infos. Drop these assignments, so
    the offset stays after the element header and only moves forward, and
    dissect nested messages (v4 error too) in a subset tvb of their own
    length, so that offsets and lengths are relative to the inner message.
    The top level dissectors also use a subset tvb of the header length,
    as the Exported PDU tvb can be longer than the message.

    Nested messages (error, requestforward, bundle_add) had no recursion
    limit, so a single PDU with thousands of nested headers overflowed the
    stack in v4, v5 and v6. Count the nesting per packet with
    p_get_proto_depth()/p_set_proto_depth(), stop with an expert info
    after 4 levels, and wrap the nested call in
    increment/decrement_dissection_depth().

    Also fix small bugs: the v5 bundle property did not advance the offset
    over type and length, the v5 empty match (length 4) was reported as too
    short, the v6 OXS experimenter value is bytes and not a 32 bit
    integer (and is bounded), and the experimenter queue stats property
    expert items in v5 and v6 used the message length instead of the
    property length.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 2815b00f70d2fd836876b5347e319c6e59cb2dd0)
    [Backport: kept 4.x epan/ipproto.h and added epan/proto_data.h for the per-packet nesting counter; the master-only epan/iana-info.h include is not needed on 4.6/4.4. Loop/recursion bodies applied cleanly.]

