commit b78a5c2425
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 18:54:24 2026 +1000

    OCP.1: Bound the PDU size to avoid an endless loop

    The 32-bit PDU size was used unchecked. A size such as 0xFFFFFFF5 made
    get_ocp1_message_len() (TCP) and dissect_ocp1_pdu()/dissect_ocp1() (UDP)
    advance the offset by a value that wraps back to 0, so the same PDUs
    were dissected forever. The size must now be at least the rest of the
    header, the sum of the sizes must not wrap, and in the UDP path the PDU
    must lie inside the remaining data. Otherwise the loop stops, and the
    UDP path adds an invalid length expert info. Every step now advances by
    at least the header size and stays in the tvb.

    Also use two case labels for Command and CommandRrq instead of
    (A || B), which evaluated to 1, and use the message offset for the
    OcaLibVolType id and the OcaTaskStatus error code, which were shown at
    the start of the parent structure.

    Assisted-by: Claude
