commit b2f6abb95a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 12:37:10 2026 +1000

    IPSec: Fix several memory-safety problems with SA configuration

    After a libgcrypt error the cipher handle was closed but
    cipher_hd_created stayed true, so the next packet of the SA used a
    freed handle. Clear the flag after every gcry_cipher_close() in the
    error paths. TWOFISH-CBC also never set the block length, so the block
    size check was skipped and every packet with a bad length failed in
    gcry_cipher_decrypt(); set it to 16.

    The IPv6 SA address filter parser could write before the start of a
    stack buffer and past its end for groups longer than four hex digits.
    Bound every write and reject such groups. The IPv4 parser applied the
    netmask with sscanf() before the expanded address was NUL-terminated,
    which read uninitialized stack memory. Terminate it first, and in both
    parsers read only the one hex digit being masked.

    Also look up the algorithm names with val_to_str_const() since the
    value_string arrays are not indexed by value, update firstValidSN only
    on the first pass, and do the AH length shift on an unsigned value.

