commit 1a6bb1923c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 16:28:30 2026 -0500

    Diameter: Bound grouped AVP recursion

    Grouped AVPs were dissected recursively without any bound, so a message
    with deeply nested grouped AVPs over the default TCP/SCTP port 3868
    overflowed the stack, also without a tree. Track the nesting with
    increment_dissection_depth()/decrement_dissection_depth().

    grouped_avp() also cleared the grouped state (dis_gouped and the
    Vendor-Id) to zero when a nested grouped AVP ended, so the AVPs after it
    in the enclosing group were treated as top level. Save and restore the
    enclosing group's state instead, and undo the depth and the state when
    an exception leaves a grouped AVP, so that the next PDU of the same TCP
    segment does not start with a higher depth.

