commit ceb5f1d27a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 16:21:57 2026 -0500

    SMB: Do not export uninitialized heap memory in Export Objects

    Export Objects could write uninitialized heap memory into an exported
    file: the per-file buffer was allocated with g_try_malloc() and the
    parts of a file between the chunks that were actually seen were never
    initialized, so they were written out as whatever the heap held.
    Likewise, once a chunk too far into the file had made the buffer be
    dropped (is_out_of_memory), a later chunk started a fresh buffer and
    reconstructed only part of the file.

    Allocate the buffer with g_try_malloc0(), zero the newly grown part
    when the buffer is enlarged, and do not start a new buffer once the
    content has been dropped.

    Assisted-by: Claude

    (backported from commit 610c8d81e3ecaf4e62501cc38f27b314c3ccd671)
    [Backport: extracted only the Export Objects memory-safety change from
     the upstream commit.]

commit 747420ba99
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 12:37:10 2026 +1000

    IPv6: Fix NULL dereference and bounds errors in extension headers

    The routing type sub-dissectors (type 0, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6) cast their
    data argument to struct ws_rthdr and dereferenced it without a check.
    Exported PDU calls any dissector reached through a uint dissector table
    with NULL data, so a crafted Exported PDU packet crashed Wireshark.
    Return 0 when data is NULL.

    The CRH dissector read one SID past the end of the header after the last
    SID, so every CRH whose SIDs were all non-zero ended up malformed and
    the payload after it was never dissected. Fetch each SID at the top of
    the loop, bounded by the SID count and the remaining length.

    The Line-Identification option with an option length of 0 computed a
    length of 0xffffffff and stepped the offset back by one byte. Report it
    with an expert info and stop.

    opt_start was a uint8_t and truncated option offsets larger than 255,
    so the undecoded remainder of an option was dissected as new options.
    Make it an int.

    The hop-by-hop, destination options, routing and fragment header
    dissectors cast their data to ws_ip6 although they can be reached from
    IPv4. Use WS_IP6_PTR() so other data is treated as no IPv6 header.

    ipv6_opt_type_hdr() kept its position in the option table in a static
    pointer, so after the first option type not in the table every lookup
    returned "any header" and the header mismatch warnings appeared in the
    first pass only. Start each lookup at the beginning of the table.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit d65c2b7bd2f52f2d009c48ff16b35652d80e01cc)
    [Backport: only dissect_routing6_srh conflicted (NULL check added, offset
