commit ee3664dcf8
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 08:00:37 2026 +1000

    LZ77: Limit the decompressed size, do not read literals past the input

    Each match of Plain LZ77 can be up to 4 GB long, and only one match was
    limited to 16 MB, so a few octets of matches expanded to gigabytes: a
    746 octet MAPI RPC_HEADER_EXT took 2.1 GB and 24 seconds to decompress,
    and a full 64 KB field about 4 GB, for every such frame. SMB2, HTTP and
    NETLOGON use the same decompressor. Limit the whole output to 16 MB. A
    literal after the end of the compressed data was read from the octets
    after it; fail instead, as [MS-XCA] does not allow it.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 9dae068965b3e92e84d7e63dc26023987a702cce)
    [Backport: 4.4 has the older byte-by-byte match-copy loop, so only the
    output-size limit was applied, not master's unrelated block-copy
    rewrite.]

