commit c07689076c
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 10:19:17 2026 +1000

    BT L2CAP: Allocate the SDU as it arrives, fix several lengths

    Each I-frame with SAR=Start allocated a file-scope buffer of the SDU
    length it claims, up to 64 KB, whatever data followed. A capture of
    small Start frames took about 4.5 KB of memory per 16-octet frame and
    gigabytes of address space. Copy what the Start frame carries and grow
    the buffer as continuation frames arrive.

    With the 4-octet extended control field the payload length still
    subtracted a 2-octet one, so the FCS was read past the frame and valid
    frames were malformed.

