commit 3ca0819578
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 16:22:14 2026 +1000

    FCSP: Fix negotiate loop and subtree placement

    dissect_fcsp_auth_negotiate() added the 32-bit parameter length from
    the packet to the offset without checking it. A length such as
    0xFFFFFFFC wrapped the offset back to the length field, and the loop
    over up to 2^32 protocols reread it until the tree item limits ended
    the dissection with a dissector bug. Stop the list with a new
    malformed expert info when the length goes beyond the packet. The
    offset in the DH-CHAP challenge handler is now unsigned like the
    others.

    The per-opcode handlers were given the top level tree instead of the
    FC-SP tree, so their items were placed outside the FC-SP subtree.

    An unknown DH-CHAP parameter tag with a non-zero length did not advance
    the offset, so the next iteration decoded the value of the unknown
    parameter as a tag. Skip the value, and count the parameter header
    against the remaining length as the known tags do.

