commit f86be82155
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 21:00:01 2026 +1000

    MySQL: Fix an infinite loop and a reassembly assertion

    A MariaDB COM_STMT_BULK_EXECUTE for a statement prepared with zero
    parameters never advanced the offset: the row loop only moves forward
    through the per-parameter inner loop, which runs zero times. Any
    trailing byte after the bulk flags then kept the dissector looping
    forever (a CPU hang, or with a tree an unbounded number of row items).
    Stop the row loop when a row consumed no bytes.

    When a decompressed PDU header was split across two compressed packets,
    dissect_mysql_decompressed_pdus() asked for the missing header bytes
    without setting desegment_offset, so a stale offset from an earlier PDU
    made the streaming reassembly code fail an assertion. Set the offset to
    the start of the partial header.

