commit 532b097e17
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 21:00:00 2026 +1000

    MIH: Fix composite tvb leak and NAI-encoded MIHF ID lengths

    dissect_mih_tlv() built a composite tvb for a MIHF ID starting with a
    backslash, outside any TRY block. The length guard measured from the
    start of the tvb instead of the field, so the first
    tvb_new_subset_length() could throw before any member was appended.
    The composite was then never chained to a parent and leaked for every
    crafted packet. Require that the whole ID exists with
    tvb_bytes_exist(tvb, offset + 1, mihf_id_len) so the loop cannot throw.

    The accepted lengths were 12, 64 and 128, which do not match the NAI
    encoding of a MAC address, IPv4 and IPv6 address (two characters per
    octet: 12, 8 and 32). Use 12, 8 and 32.

