commit 4d94dc5fe5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 19:03:59 2026 +1000

    NR-RRC: Bound recursion through nested NR RRC messages

    The MRDC transfer messages ULInformationTransferMRDC and
    DLInformationTransferMRDC carry a complete UL-DCCH-Message or
    DL-DCCH-Message as an octet string, which was dissected by calling the
    message dissector directly. A packet in which each level contains the
    same message type again needs only about four bytes per level, so a
    packet of a few kilobytes overflowed the stack. This is reachable by
    default through LTE RRC and NR RRC.

    Allow at most 8 nested NR RRC messages per packet and stop with an
    expert info (nr-rrc.nesting_too_deep) beyond that; count each nested
    message as a dissection level too. The same limit now also guards the
    existing segment reassembly recursion, which called
    increment_dissection_depth() without checking the limit and could end
    in an assertion.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
