commit 8d9162ec90
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 19:03:59 2026 +1000

    MAC-NR: Fix use after free on an unknown framing tag

    dissect_mac_nr_context_fields() freed the mac_nr_info on an unknown
    context tag and then returned true. Both callers took that as success,
    stored the freed pointer with p_add_proto_data() and went on to read it
    in dissect_mac_nr(); mac-nr-framed also wrote into and freed it again on
    the next pass. That is a heap use after free and a double free.

    Return false without freeing instead. Each caller now frees the struct
    only if it allocated it in this call; mac-nr-framed never frees a struct
    it got back from p_get_proto_data(). Nothing is stored before the
    context parse succeeded.

