commit 10da242959
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 12:30:39 2026 +1000

    LISP: Bound LCAF address recursion and fix a depth leak

    get_addr_str() recursed through nested Instance ID and AS Number LCAFs
    with only increment_dissection_depth(), so a chain of nested LCAFs ran
    into the dissection depth assertion. The recursion now goes through a
    static helper with a level counter and stops at 4 levels, returning a
    placeholder string.

    dissect_lcaf() returned from the unknown LCAF type case without calling
    decrement_dissection_depth(), leaking one level per such LCAF. It now
    skips the data and leaves through the common exit.

    dissect_lcaf_afi_list() returned -1 for an unknown AFI, which callers
    used as an offset. It now returns the current offset after the expert
    info. dissect_lcaf_nonce_loc() used tvb_get_ntohl() for the one byte
    reserved field and the three byte nonce, reading past them. Strings
    returned by get_addr_str() can be NULL for an unknown AFI; they are
    now replaced by "(unknown)" when appended to the tree item text.

