commit 721eaca9c0
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 12:30:39 2026 +1000

    LDAP: Fix a NULL tvb, quadratic filter strings and small bugs

    An empty constructed OCTET STRING as an AttributeValue leaves no
    tvbuff, and the default and the custom attribute UAT paths then passed
    NULL to tvb_ascii_isprint() or proto_tree_add_item(), which hits a
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT. Return early when there is no tvb.

    The display string of a SubstringFilter was rebuilt with
    wmem_strdup_printf() for every substring item, so the packet pool grew
    quadratically (63 KB of items used 530 MB). Build it in a wmem_strbuf
    instead and stop appending once it holds ITEM_LABEL_LENGTH (240)
    characters; a single item contributes at most that many characters.

