commit ec417b6401
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 12:30:39 2026 +1000

    LBMPDM: Fix crashes and hangs on malformed messages

    A DECIMAL field with an exponent of -64 or less made the divisor
    10^n wrap to zero, so the modulo that followed raised SIGFPE. The
    positive exponent path and the negation of INT64_MIN also overflowed
    signed arithmetic. Exponents with an absolute value above 18 are now
    shown raw, and the arithmetic uses unsigned magnitudes with an
    overflow check.

    An offset table entry with a huge field id (up to 0x7fffffff) made the
    dissector allocate and fill an array of that many entries, up to 8 GiB
    from a 32 byte packet. Ids above 65535 now get an expert info and the
    table is dropped. Offset table segments are also checked against the
    reported length of the packet before the arrays sized by the segment
    length are allocated. Offsets from the table that point outside the
    data segment are skipped.

    The segment length was converted to a signed int and could become zero
    or negative, so the segment loop never advanced. The loop now rejects
    segments shorter than the segment header or longer than the message
    remainder or the packet, with an expert info. A message length smaller
    than the message header, which wrapped the remaining length, is
    rejected too.

    An array field whose elements have zero size iterated up to 2^32
    times at the same offset. The loop now stops with an expert info.

    The length of a string-named field definition (uint32 + 4) could wrap
    to zero so the definition loop did not advance. It must now be at
    least the minimum definition size and fit in the segment; otherwise
    the loop stops with an expert info.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit f79a39894c9388878fb781de7f76172db11a3053)

commit e93bca08fa
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 12:30:39 2026 +1000

    L2TP: Fix session list growth and Ericsson AVP length handling

    update_session() appended the session to tunnel->sessions on every
    call, even when an existing entry was found and merely updated, and it
    ran on every dissection pass. A capture with many control messages
    built a list with duplicate entries, making each find_session() walk
    longer and the total work quadratic. Append only newly created
    sessions, and call update_session() only on the first pass.

    The Ericsson TEI to SC Map AVP created its subset with avp_len instead
    of avp_len - 1 after consuming the map count byte, so the subset could
    extend past the AVP. Require avp_len >= 1 and use avp_len - 1.

    The Ericsson Transport Configuration AVP subtracted 3 from avp_len
    without checking it, which underflows for short AVPs. Report a bad AVP
    length with the existing expert info when avp_len < 3.

