commit 65e8a28437
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 19:55:21 2026 +1000

    KT: Check the key, value, name and log sizes against the packet

    The ksiz, vsiz, nsiz and size fields are 32-bit values taken from the
    packet and were passed unchecked as the length of proto_tree_add_item()
    and added to an int offset. A value of 0xFFFFFFFF became the length -1,
    which means "to the end of the data", and moved the offset back by one
    byte. With a large record count every record then added the rest of the
    packet to the tree twice, which needs memory quadratic in the packet
    size.

    Call tvb_ensure_bytes_exist64() before every item whose length comes
    from the packet, so that a size larger than the remaining data ends the
    dissection with an exception instead.

