commit 83664b49e1
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 19:55:21 2026 +1000

    ISO 15765: Do not assert on too many segments, clamp the length

    The per-sequence-number counter of segments was a uint8_t that wrapped
    after 255 consecutive frames with the same 4-bit sequence number, and
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT(frag_id_high != 0) then aborted the dissection. This
    is reachable from a crafted LIN diagnostic capture. Check the counter
    before incrementing it; at UINT8_MAX add a new expert info and flag the
    transfer as being in error instead.

