commit accaf55a55
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 12:37:09 2026 +1000

    iperf3: Do not mix TCP and UDP conversation data

    The TCP and the UDP dissector store differently sized structures under
    the same protocol key of a conversation found by address and port only.
    A packet reaching the UDP dissector through Exported PDU with the
    addresses and ports of a TCP iperf3 flow got the 12 byte TCP structure
    and used it as the UDP one, reading past the allocation and using the
    bytes as a map pointer. The reverse mixed the UDP structure into the TCP
    sequence state and could hit a DISSECTOR_ASSERT_NOT_REACHED.

    Return early unless pinfo->ptype is PT_TCP in the TCP dissector and
    PT_UDP in the UDP dissector.

