Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 18:55:34 2026 +1000

    H.245: Reset the H.223 channel parameters for every OpenLogicalChannel

    The forward and reverse H.223 logical channel parameters are kept in
    file-scope pointers that were never reset. An OpenLogicalChannel
    without reverse parameters therefore inherited those of an earlier
    one, and its OpenLogicalChannelAck then failed the DISSECTOR_ASSERT
    that compares the reverse channel of the ack and the request. The
    pointers also outlived the file-scope memory they point to.

    Reset both pointers at the start of each OpenLogicalChannel and when
    the file is closed, and replace the assertion, whose two sides both
