commit f9ffb35cba
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 17:39:52 2026 +1000

    GVSP: Limit the work done for GenDC component and part offsets

    The GenDC container descriptor was decoded by following the component
    offset array and, for each component, its part offset array. Nothing
    prevented the offsets from repeating, so a packet of 64 KB made the
    dissector decode N * P part headers, which takes seconds and exhausts
    the tree item limit.

    Require the component offsets and the part offsets of one component to
    increase strictly, limit the total number of part headers to 1024 and
    stop with an expert info otherwise.

    The component and part header subtrees also added offset + 16 twice,
    so they started in the wrong place. Use the already adjusted offsets.

    Assisted-by: Claude
