commit f7704efa5d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 08:49:38 2026 +1000

    GELF: Fix a memory leak when a chunked message is truncated

    The chunked message ID was fetched into a GByteArray that was only
    freed after later calls, which can throw on a short packet. The array
    then leaked. Copy the eight ID bytes into a stack buffer instead.

    BUILD_MESSAGE_ID() shifted the message id bytes by 3, 2, 1 and 0 bits
    instead of 24, 16, 8 and 0, which made different chunked messages share
    a reassembly id. Build the 32 bit value with the right shifts.

