commit bf9d881d61
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 16:22:14 2026 +1000

    f5ethtrailer: Fix noise asserts and short trailer handling

    The "f5ethtrailer.noise" dissector can be called by name, for example
    from an Exported PDU file, with a NULL data argument. The noise
    subdissectors then hit DISSECTOR_ASSERT(tdata != NULL) and the frame
    shows a dissector bug. Return 0 for missing data in the entry point
    and replace the three assertions with plain checks.

    The heuristic subtracted the offset of the first non-zero byte from
    a trailer length that was already measured from that offset. With
    the unsigned wrap the size test passed on short remainders, and the
    FCS probe read past the end of the tvb, so a frame that is not an
    F5 trailer showed as malformed. Test the remaining length instead,
    and compare the DPT length against what remains from the magic,
    which also covers the case where the trailer starts after an FCS.

    An RST cause length of 1 to 8 made the string and item lengths negative
    in the old medium trailers and in the DPT medium v4 noise. Reject such
    lengths (treat them as bad in v4). The v3 RST cause length was read with
    a signed accessor; use tvb_get_uint8. In the low noise v2/v3 VIP name,
    the length check now starts at the name, one byte after the length.

    dissect_dpt_trailer() returned a DPT length smaller than the header,
    or larger than the data, as is; use the tvb length in that case
    so the heuristic does not return after adding items. A '%' in the
    brief_inout_chars preference produced an invalid printf format and
    is now rejected in favour of the default characters.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit 1a8b90d57e10401b1c2315352aaf17cb09ef5d8f)

