commit 5f6965635e
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 08:50:17 2026 +1000

    RBM: Decode Ruby Marshal integers like Ruby does

    get_rbm_integer() left its value and length outputs unset for the
    type byte 0xfa (-6), so an Array or Hash used an uninitialised element
    count and the offset moved by an uninitialised length. This is reached
    by default when a Ruby Marshal file is opened, and in DRb.

    The function also differed from r_long() in Ruby's marshal.c for the
    type bytes 4 (a 4-byte positive integer, decoded as -1) and -5 (0,
    decoded as a 5-byte integer with an undefined shift). Decode all type
    bytes as Ruby does, so every path sets both outputs, and build the
    multi-byte values in an unsigned integer.

    dissect_rbm_inline() left its type and value outputs unset when the
    header version was not supported, and DRb then used them.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (cherry picked from commit e5381a5c60d6e665fdcd8d717c3b7405bc38be48)

