commit 496192c15a
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 17:39:50 2026 +1000

    GSM A BSSMAP: Bound Field Element recursion and fix small errors

    The Cell Load Information Group field element (0x0b) is dissected by
    be_fe_cell_load_info_group(), which calls be_field_element_dissect(),
    which can dispatch to the same element again. The length of a field
    element was not checked against the enclosing element, so a packet
    could nest it without limit and overflow the stack, or hit the maximum
    tree depth. Stop with an expert info when the nesting gets too deep,
    stop when the cell id used up the whole element, and clamp the length
    of each field element to what is left of the enclosing element.

    be_res_avail() read a 32 bit value into a 16 bit variable, used the same
    value for the full rate and half rate counts, and set the item length to
    the length of the whole element. Read each 2 octet count separately,
    make the fields FT_UINT16 and drop the proto_item_set_len() calls.

    be_speech_codec_lst() and be_speech_codec() set the length of the last
    item only once after the loop. Set it for each item in the loop.

    [pinfo->dissection_depth is an int on this branch, so the comparison
    with prefs.gui_max_tree_depth casts the latter to int, as packet.c
    does, to avoid a -Wsign-compare warning. The expert info table
    conflicted only because this branch lacks the unrelated spacing change
    to the extraneous data message.]

