commit ffd3bb20b5
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 10:03:47 2026 +1000

    DCOM: Limit nested OBJREFs, register custom marshalers for every packet

    A custom OBJREF is handed to the marshaler of its interface, and some
    marshalers, such as the one for IStorage, dissect an OBJREF again, so a
    request with nested custom OBJREFs recursed until the stack overflowed
    and tshark crashed. Count each custom OBJREF in the dissection depth.

    The custom marshalers of ISystemActivator and WMIO were registered only
    when an activation or IWbemServices call was dissected, so an OBJREF in
    an earlier frame was not decoded on the first pass but was on the
    second. Register them when a file is opened. A handler OBJREF stored the
    IPID of its standard OBJREF in the IID.

    A VARIANT of type VT_CY decoded its value with field index 0 and failed
    an assertion on any such VARIANT. Decode it without a field.

