commit e162dc501d
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 08:49:37 2026 +1000

    ForCES: Fix cubic time in nested LFB select TLV loops

    The LFBselect TLV loop called dissect_operation_tlv(), which itself
    looped over Operation TLVs up to the end of the tvbuff, and each of
    those called dissect_path_data_tlv(), which again looped to the end of
    the tvbuff. A packet of a few KB of small TLVs therefore took O(N^3)
    time (6 KB took about 9 seconds).

    Make dissect_operation_tlv() handle exactly one Operation TLV, with a
    length check, and give dissect_path_data_tlv() a subset tvbuff
    limited to that TLV, so each level only walks its own TLV. The tree
    for valid packets is unchanged. Stop the LFBselect loop on a TLV
    length below the TLV header size.

    [The Operation TLV type is read with tvb_get_ntohs() on this branch
    rather than with proto_tree_add_item_ret_uint(); the fix's version of
    dissect_operation_tlv() is used as is.]

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 1e2fb3338a7832d8bcdb77b83a2e20dd294d715a)

