commit 93498e1eb9
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 19:59:11 2026 -0500

    DNS: Clear all of the client subnet address (union initialization)

    The address of an EDNS Client Subnet option is copied into a union of a
    uint32_t and 16 octets, initialized with {0}. Strictly according to the
    C standard since C99 (and explictly since C23) that initializes only the
    first member. GCC 15 and later and Clang 18 and later* no longer clear the
    rest of a union with automatic storage, so the last 12 octets are
    uninitialized on some compilers, including the latest GCC. (There's
    a -fzero-init-padding-bits=unions flag but we don't seem to have
    anywhere else in the code that does this with a union specifically
    so it's probably best to fix it.)

    C23 has {} which we might use eventually.

    This was exposed by the test in e139bcf392431805e13a1f0f5bbf25b0c30cca89
    and also running the test on very recent GCC.

    * - Technically, the LLVM first step treated the rest of the bytes as
    uninitialized, but the backend would zero out the rest.

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 helped run this down

    (cherry picked from commit 958b219effa4ae9f788e87807e85dfa1c36a4264)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

commit f213fe6b01
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 16:52:54 2026 +1000

    ESS: Reset the security category OID for each category

    object_identifier_id is a file-scope pointer that is set to a string
    in pinfo->pool by the SecurityCategory type and the tagName fields,
    and was never reset. A SecurityCategory without its [0] type still
    reaches the [1] value, which then looked up the OID string of an
    earlier packet after that packet's pool had been freed, a heap use
    after free. The ess_dissect_attribute() and
    ess_dissect_attribute_flags() helpers compared the same stale pointer,
    or NULL, with strcmp() when a tag set had no tagName and the "ESS
    Category Attributes" table had entries.

    Reset the pointer to NULL at the start of SecurityCategory,
    RestrictiveTag, EnumeratedTag, PermissiveTag and InformativeTag, and
    skip the attribute name lookup when no OID has been seen.
    call_ber_oid_callback() already handles a NULL OID.

