commit 7a58ef9609
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 21:07:38 2026 -0500

    epan: Check for label overflow on FT_DOUBLE both before and after units

    80f16015e2af296fb5ab8f676979bfed9731171f introduced new float display
    types. Unfortunately I expect that some people may reach for BASE_DEC as
    the "standard" choice, but really for most purposes BASE_NONE is better.
    In particular, BASE_DEC can overflow the standard label width.

    The ability to append units was added to FT_FLOAT and FT_DOUBLE, but
    as sprintf and g_strlcpy return the size of the attempted result,
