commit fd6e44c8c3
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 16:43:55 2026 +1000

    CAST: Do not let the PDU length wrap

    get_cast_pdu_len() added the header length to the data length in 32
    bits, so a data length close to 4 GiB gave a PDU length of 0 or a few
    octets. A length of 0 made TCP add every later segment of the stream
    to the same PDU and dissect all of it again for each one, which takes
    quadratic time. Return a length shorter than the header instead, which
    is reported as malformed.

