commit ef69398e43
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 09:14:11 2026 +1000

    Aeron: Don't add fragments to a message that is already complete

    With fragment reassembly enabled, a message that was already complete
    still took the next contiguous fragment, and a retransmitted begin
    fragment was added to it again. Each fragment with the end flag then
    rebuilt the whole message in a new file scope buffer, so memory grew
    with the square of the number of fragments: a 1.3 MB capture used
    6.4 GB.

    Ignore a retransmitted begin fragment of a complete message, and keep
    other fragments that follow a complete message as orphans. Also build
    the frame info lookup key on the stack; the key values were leaked on
    every lookup.

