commit 34ada27af9
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 10:27:21 2026 +1000

    Bitcoin: Do not wrap the PDU length, check varint lengths

    get_bitcoin_pdu_length() added the 24 octet header to the 32-bit
    payload length, so a payload length of 0xffffffe8 gave a PDU length
    of 0, which TCP takes as "one more segment": every later segment of
    the stream was added and the whole buffer dissected again, quadratic
    in the length of the stream (8000 segments took 11 s). The heuristic
    is enabled by default. Return the largest length instead.

    String, data, addrv2 address, witness component and merkleblock flag
    lengths are varints that were cut to 32 bits, so 0xffffffff became -1,
    "to the end of the tvb", and the offset stepped back one octet. Throw
    when such a length is longer than what is left.

    Also put the header length macro in parentheses, and pass ENC_NA
    instead of the display flag BASE_SHOW_UTF_8_PRINTABLE as the encoding
    of two FT_BYTES fields.

