commit 6f1e7252a2
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 03:03:21 2026 +1000

    Couchbase: Check 32-bit value lengths, limit the JSON results

    The 32-bit lengths of multipath values and results, DCP cache transfer
    items and xattrs were passed as int lengths and added to the offset. A
    length of 0xFFFFFFFF became -1, which means "to the end" and does not
    throw, and moved the offset back one octet. Each spec then added an item
    holding the rest of the PDU while moving forward only a few octets, so a
    60 KB frame used 1.5 GB with a tree and a 250 KB one 5.2 GB. The value
    length of a frame, the body length minus the other sections, wrapped the
    same way. Throw when a length does not fit in the packet.

    Every multipath result was handed to the JSON dissector, which adds a
    layer each time, so about 490 results hit the DISSECTOR_ASSERT on the
    number of layers in call_dissector_work(). Stop calling it before the
    limit.

    When the path of a subdoc value was longer than the value, the value
    length wrapped and the value took the rest of the PDU.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
    (backported from commit 1492169519551013720ed95e26b1acc375d837d2)

commit bc8cbf0f3e
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 2 05:34:07 2026 -0500

    COSE: Do not crash without media information, do not leak a header key

    The application/cose media type handle read the media parameters from
    its data argument without checking it. AMQP 0-9 content bodies, OBEX and
    ID3v2 pictures call the media_type table with no media_content_info_t
    and a type taken from the packet, so an AMQP message with the content
    type application/cose crashed tshark.

    When the principal key of a header map was found, its value was read
    before the key was released. If the value was missing, the exception
    skipped the release and the GVariant leaked.

    A cose-type media parameter that is not in the subtype table gave a
    NULL handle, which was passed to call_dissector_only() and hit its
    DISSECTOR_ASSERT, for example for an HTTP body with an unknown
    cose-type. Show the invalid tag expert info instead. An unsigned
    content format was added to an FT_INT64 field with
    proto_tree_add_cbor_uint64(), which is a dissector bug; make the field
    FT_UINT64.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

