commit a133b60f36
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 16:33:53 2026 +1000

    CIP: Keep the embedded and multiple service requests apart

    The request info of a CIP request kept the requests of a Multiple
    Service Packet and the request embedded in an Unconnected Send in the
    same pointer. ENIP passes the request's info to a frame in the other
    direction, so a frame that carried an Unconnected Send request after a
    Multiple Service Packet request used the 16 octet multiple service
    info as a 64 octet request info and wrote past its end. Keep the two
    in separate fields.

    The same frame order with a Forward Open request asserted that the
    request had no connection yet. Keep the connection of the first
    request instead.

    Do not allocate request info for more services than the packet has
    offsets for, and take the size of the additional status of a PCCC
    response from the additional status size instead of the general
    status.

