commit 6a9255fab1
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 06:29:59 2026 -0500

    Ceph: Do not let lengths move the offset back, fix field types

    A PDU length or authorizer length that wrapped the end of the PDU back
    to its start made dissect_ceph() dissect the same PDU forever, saving
    new state each time. Stop at a PDU end that does not move forward.

    An encoded struct whose size ran past the end of the data, or a
    snapinfo that returned its encoded size instead of its end, moved the
    offset back, which asserted with a tree and looped over the same bytes
    up to four billion times without one. Throw when the size does not
    fit, and continue after the end of the snapinfo.

    When the first pass stopped at the start of a frame, no state was
    saved for it and later passes asserted. Start from a new state then.

    Adding the high flags of a pool from an empty list of fields was a
    dissector bug for every OSD map with a pool, and an object locator
    with both a key and a hash added an expert info without a tvb, which
    asserted. Add the high flags as a plain value, give the low flags
    their own subtree, and add the expert info at the locator.

    The redirect object name and the PG stats category are strings, and
    the Pool Op Reply data is a container; their field types asserted or
    were reported as malformed. Also label the snapinfo instead of
    replacing its text, and end each mon subscription item.

