commit eb7f00237e
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:40:11 2026 -0400

    dumpcap: Reset the options parser before parsing the log options

    The ws_getopt_long() loop that looks for -Z and the application flavor
    goes through all of the arguments, and ws_log_parse_args() was called
    after it without resetting the options parser, so it didn't see any
    arguments. --log-level, --log-file and the other log options had no
    effect, and invalid values for them were silently accepted, e.g.
    "dumpcap --log-level=bogus -v" printed the version and exited with 0.

    Set ws_optreset and ws_optind to 1 first, as tshark does.

