commit b27afa02c1
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 08:45:46 2026 -0400

    ADB Service: Don't carry over a logcat entry longer than 5 KiB

    When a logcat message is not complete, the bytes received so far are
    kept in file scope and put in front of the next message's data. Each
    message that still doesn't complete the entry keeps its own copy of
    everything received so far, so memory grows with the square of the
    number of messages. A payload length of 0xFFFF with one byte in each
    following message made a 6 MB capture use 2.3 GB.

    Android limits a log entry, header included, to 5 KiB
    (LOGGER_ENTRY_MAX_LEN). Report a longer entry as malformed and don't
    keep it for the next message.

    Assisted-by: Claude

    (backported from commit b669f03cd5f814f83e944a661a5ec094f75a1134)

    Co-authored-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

