Date:   Fri Oct 30 08:57:19 2026 -0400

    BT HCI ISO: Check the data argument, fix stray and timestamped fragments

    "bthci_iso_data" is a registered handle, so an Exported PDU file can
    call it without iso_data_info_t; it then dereferenced NULL. Return 0
    instead, and drop the dead assertion in the main dissector.

    A reassembled SDU was decoded with the TS flag of the last fragment,
    which is always clear, so the time stamp was shown as the sequence
    number and SDU length; keep the flag of the first fragment. A
    continuation or last fragment after a completed SDU, or after a first
    fragment that was rejected, attached itself to that SDU and decoded it
    again; ignore an SDU that was completed in an earlier frame. Read the
    SDU length of a first fragment on every pass, so a short fragment is
    malformed with tshark -2 as well.

