commit 2d8230ff69
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 23:56:51 2026 -0400

    ACN: Build the universe discovery list in a wmem_strbuf

    The sACN universe discovery list was built in a 97-byte buffer, one
    universe after another, but every snprintf() call was given the size
    of the whole buffer rather than the space left after the write
    pointer. No universe list wrote past the end, but a build with
    _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, which CMakeLists.txt sets for all but Debug builds,
    checks the size against the space left and aborts ("buffer overflow
    detected") on the second universe. A discovery packet listing two or
    more universes made tshark abort.

    Append the universes to a wmem_strbuf instead, so no size has to be
    tracked.

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

