commit ce2da16286
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 21:17:37 2026 -0400

    ACN: Bound the DMP address ranges shown for a single data item

    A DMP range address with a single data item (D_RS) shows the item once
    for every address in the range, without advancing through the packet,
    so a 32-bit count taken from the packet decided how many strings were
    allocated. A 170-byte packet made tshark allocate memory until it was
    killed. A range with an array of equal size items (D_RE) whose count
    was larger than its data length gave an item size of zero and the same
    loop.

    Show at most 1024 addresses of a D_RS range, in both data and reason
    codes, and add an expert info when the range is longer. Decode a D_RE
    range item by item only when every item has at least one byte. Stop
    mapping virtual addresses when one doesn't advance the offset, and
    show the range increment and count as unsigned.

