commit 92572bea27
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 28 18:08:00 2026 -0400

    AMQP: Store prop_flags in a uint32_t to prevent UB on Windows

    Since the C integer promotions turn uint16_t into int, retrieving
    the prop_flags and storing it in a uint16_t, and then repeatedly
    left-shifting to test against 0x8000 is UB, as left-shifting a
    negative signed number is UB.

    This is the shortest fix; it would probably be better to avoid the
    left shifts entirely, use defines for the masks, and also add
    individual fields for the flag bits in the header for clarity.

    (cherry picked from commit 3c812870a53f06e136e798b57aa3fad97cfa698f)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

