commit 0af2d309ff
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 17:26:12 2026 -0400

    TLS: Check for transcript length overflow

    The handshake transcript (kept in [D]TLS 1.2 for the Extended
    Master Secret) is appended to with a 32-bit length and no overflow
    check. A connection with more than 4 GiB of handshake messages (e.g.,
    many handshake messages before the master secret is known, which is
    always the case when the keys aren't available) wraps the length, and
    the next copy writes past the end of the buffer. Check for that, and
    don't append to a transcript that would overflow.

    4.4 doesn't have the Encrypted Client Hello transcript from #21693.

    Related to #21693

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

    (backported from commit eb6fdfd82527d9ef6755d204262fa297610e8c38)

