commit 310fac68fd
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 15:19:39 2026 -0400

    BT HCI ACL, BT HCI ISO: Grow reassembly buffers as data arrives

    The first fragment of a PDU allocated a file scope buffer for the
    entire length claimed in its header (up to 64 KiB for ACL), even if no
    more fragments arrive, so a capture of tiny first fragments uses far
    more memory than its size. Grow the buffer as fragments are added
    instead, doubling in size up to the total length.

    Also, the ACL total length (L2CAP length + 4) was stored in 16 bits,
    so the largest L2CAP PDUs could never be reassembled.

    Thanks to AISLE Security for the report

    Fix #21656

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    (cherry picked from commit b99adb99fb6e257a5a1bbc7fdb599cdc59c629d5)

