commit 8f84ab33e2
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 18:53:33 2026 -0400

    BGP: Finish dissecting path attributes after an invalid length

    dissect_bgp_path_attr() returning early for an invalid path attribute
    length skips decrementing the dissection depth. That's not ideal, though
    generally a low impact issue. Mildly more impactful if skipping the
    postponed dissection of a LINK_STATE attribute which came before the
