commit b1a06824a6
Author: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 18:05:59 2026 +1000

    SMB2: Fix memory safety issues found in an audit

    - SRT tap: the opcode is a 16-bit value from the packet but indexed a
      256 entry table. add_srt_table_data() only checks the index with
      ws_assert(), so release builds wrote past the end of the heap
      buffer. Skip out-of-range opcodes.
    - Compression: refuse a compression transform nested inside
      decompressed data, which could multiply the decompression memory
      use for every nesting level. Add an expert info for it.
    - Fix the chained compression check that tested a constant instead of
      the algorithm.
    - Zero-initialize export object file info, and remember it when it is
      created on a file id lookup.
    - Use the offset returned by dissect_windows_sockaddr_storage() in the
      share redirect error context instead of adding it.

