commit 088dff4362
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 23 08:58:49 2026 -0400

    systemd journal: Decode binary-safe string fields as UTF-8

    String fields serialized in the binary-safe format were added with
    ENC_NA, i.e. ASCII, so every non-ASCII byte was shown as a replacement
    character. Fields that contain a newline or other control character
    are serialized that way even when they are valid UTF-8, so e.g. a
    multi-line message with an accented character was mangled. Use
    ENC_UTF_8 as for text fields.

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    (cherry picked from commit 3ed7ad87893e2e2b8f31c98ebe6e6c18b81d248a)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

commit e218b546fb
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 17:20:36 2026 -0400

    sdjournal: Serialize entries with control codepoints as binary-safe

    The systemd journal export format, in addition to serializing journal
    fields which are not valid UTF-8 in a binary-safe manner, also uses the
    binary-safe method for fields with control codepoints. journalctl
    -o export treats as control codepoints C0 other than TAB (so including
    newline), plus DEL and C1 (U+007F to U+009F). The format documentation
    only mentions values below 32 other than TAB, but systemd 259 also
    exports fields with DEL or C1 codepoints as binary.

    https://systemd.io/JOURNAL_EXPORT_FORMATS/

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    (backported from commit 3a986b7686258218c633b04eb050fbe069d86cc2)

