commit 97e82468b2
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 09:57:05 2026 -0400

    SMB Pipe: Bound LANMAN descriptor repeat counts

    A repeat count in a LANMAN descriptor string such as "B4294967295"
    overflowed get_count() and wrapped to -1. The data dissector then
    moved the offset backwards, so the auxiliary data loops could run
    billions of iterations without advancing.

    - Cap descriptor repeat counts at 0xFFFF.
    - Stop the auxiliary data loops when an entry does not advance the
      offset.
    - Dissect auxiliary response data with the auxiliary data descriptor
      instead of the main data descriptor.
    - Stop dissecting response entries when an entry consumes no data,
      for example when the data descriptor contains only null pointers,
      and add an expert info. Otherwise every one of up to 65535 entries
      added items at the same offset.

    Fixes #21482

    Assisted-by: Claude
    Signed-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <ronniesahlberg@gmail.com>

    (cherry picked from commit e0c23bb5979edea79a30ab5a686d1c9a6d4d90df)

