commit c10ced89a8
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 20:43:50 2026 -0400

    IEEE 1905: Prevent possible buffer overflow calculating fragment hash

    The packet src and dst address when dissecting Bluetooth can be a string
    which is the concatenation of the string representation of the BDADDR
    (up to 64 bytes if name resolution is enabled) and the Bluetooth
    friendly device name (up to 248 bytes). Two of those addresses combined
    (plus 5 more bytes for other parts of the key) can overflow a uint8_t.
    Store the buffer length in a 32-bit unsigned integer so that overflow
    can never occur.

    Fix #21683

    Thanks to Anthropic's Claude and Ada Logics for the report and PoC.

    (backported from commit e099bf71c44046ef1ba39c6d0d827928a840664b)

commit dae2d4c755
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
