commit 32cac07a8d
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 12:01:52 2026 -0400

    ERF: Skip PAD blocks properly

    The ERF reader wants to completely skip PAD blocks. On the sequential
    pass, don't read the bytes from the pad blocks into the record Buffer,
    just discard them (it's still a short file if they end prematurely.)
    Unref the block created by erf_read_header for the pad block to avoid a leak.
    Update the record offset in erf_read at the start of each loop iteration,
    so that PAD blocks are ignored on the random access as well.

    It might be simpler logic in some ways to skip the pad blocks inside
    erf_read_header (it could avoid creating blocks to unref), but then
    we'd have to do more to retrieve the proper offset and avoid having to
    skip again on random access.

    Fix #21682

    Thanks to Anthropic's Claude and Ada Logics for the report and PoC.

    (backported from commit 055f2a8f5f06d93a42c27d101f414807cb466fc8)

