commit b8ef578cab
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 16 18:58:58 2026 -0400

    TFTP: Don't process option negotiation after transaction begins

    TFTP is a lockstep protocol. The option extension requires option
    negotiation prior to beginning the file transfer.[1] In particular,
    the block size should not change during the transaction. The window
    size can change in a Microsoft extension, but that is not sent in a
    OACK opcode but in ACKs.

    If an OACK appears after the data has begun, flag it as an expert info
    and don't update the conversation info data such as the blocksize.
    Also add a DISSECTOR_ASSERT to make sure that this works and we don't
    overflow the buffer.

    Also, dupe the file-scoped data in the TShark single-pass case, because
    commit 722f9eb492e9bf72e9dae50a2dea806832eb8c5c means that eo data is
    g_free'd (like how the GUI does), and we can't free file-scoped data
    that way.

    Fix #21611

    Thanks to Lia04-WD for reporting.

    1 - https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2347/

    (cherry picked from commit 36edcd1d103ceb0be6a5f9fdaee1467fc4d7dda8)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

