commit 5c29fb727f
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 07:41:09 2026 -0400

    NTLMSSP: Compute the NTLMv2 proof over the whole response

    create_ntlmssp_v2_key() copied the NTLMv2 response after the NT proof
    into a 768 byte stack buffer, using MIN() so that the copy fit, but
    then passed the untrimmed length to ws_hmac_buffer(). A response
    longer than 776 bytes (they can be up to NTLMSSP_BLOB_MAX_SIZE)
    therefore made the HMAC read past the end of the buffer. It also meant
    that legitimate responses with long AV pair lists could never be
    verified, as the proof was computed over the wrong data.

    Build the server challenge and the rest of the response in a buffer of
    the right size, once, before trying each credential.

    This requires NT credentials or an RC4 keytab entry to be configured.

    Thanks to Yuyao Jiang for reporting.

    Fix #21643

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

    (cherry picked from commit 622de8cda8205b5a7175431b52cf6d0d9f773c1c)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

commit c7adf78d16
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 21:09:42 2026 -0400

    SPNEGO: Reject an empty RC4-HMAC wrap payload when decrypting

    decrypt_arcfour() didn't check that the wrap token had any data after
    the header. With nothing there, the output buffer is a zero length
    allocation (NULL from wmem_alloc), and gssapi_verify_pad() read the
    padding length from the byte before it.

    Return an error for an empty payload, and make gssapi_verify_pad()
    reject a zero length too.

    This requires an RC4-HMAC key in the keytab that decrypts the token's
    sequence number correctly.

