commit aec9fb83be
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 11:14:40 2026 -0400

    snoop: Error before allocation if a pseudo-header size is too large

    In the Shomiti/Finisar Surveyor flavor of the snoop format, the
    pseudo-header is variable length and given in the header. If the
    pseudo-header length is larger than the total packet length, go
    ahead and fail with an error instead of allocating a very large
    Buffer after integer overflow, and then failing to read bytes.

    That Buffer is freed shortly afterwards with the failure, so this
    near-4GiB allocation is only a problem for systems that might fail
    to make the allocation.

    Use checked integer arithmetic, and make the header length unsigned.

    Thanks to AISLE Security for the report and PoC.

    (cherry picked from commit 76459b81349ecc2c1d82dec1de2e032ebf2f731f)

    Co-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>

commit 66a70bb36a
