commit 86391d0d67
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 11:08:42 2026 -0400

    wiretap: busmaster: Bound scanner tokens

    Each time Flex refills its buffer it copies the partial token to the
    start of the buffer, and refills are capped at 16 KB, so scanning an
    unbounded token takes time quadratic in its length. 10 MB of spaces
    took 23 seconds to read, and a 10 MB line in the channel section of
    the header took over a minute.

    Put an upper bound on every pattern. Skip the header's channel and
    database sections, and the text after ERR, in pieces up to the end
    of the line instead of matching the whole line as one token.

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

    (cherry picked from commit c21af83800d43e1d79da08f6603b056cc1915c0f)

