commit ebc86cf10f
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 09:34:30 2026 -0400

    wiretap: ascend: Bound scanner tokens and line length

    The scanner's YY_INPUT supplies one byte at a time, and each time Flex
    refills its buffer it copies the partial token to the start of the
    buffer, so scanning an unbounded token takes time quadratic in its
    length. Several patterns were unbounded (hex numbers, the character
    display after the hex bytes, quoted task names, the WDD call number
    and type, and others); a 400 KB run of hex digits took over nine
    minutes to read. Put an upper bound on every pattern, and consume the
    character display in pieces up to the end of the line.

    Also limit lines to 1024 characters (real lines are around 80), and
    return an error for a longer one.

    When the parser was converted from Bison to Lemon, run_ascend_parser()
    went from returning 0 on success to returning true, but its callers
    were not updated. ascend_open() could never fail on an I/O error, and
    parse_ascend() reported "no data returned by parse" for parse errors
    and vice versa. Fix both.
    Fixup f21cd2e23f372bd42e4792ef0b4294d2db881a92

    Thanks to AISLE security for a report.

    Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
    (backported from commit 08ed4cf790de9f9c7bb1ef17bbf15b2d1308f25f)

