commit 6873368472
Author: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 08:50:01 2026 -0400

    RTSE: Global proto_tree considered harmful

    The proto_tree objects are automatically freed at the end of a frame;
    having them dissector level globals leads to a possibility of use after
    free when a dissector has multiple entry points, some of which are PDUs
    called by other dissectors where top_tree is intended to be NULL. The
    old top tree might not get set to NULL when an exception occurs.

    Set it in proto_data for the protocol, which cleans up automatically at
    the correct time.  Make the indentation somewhat more consistent.

    Fix #21585. Thanks to Antti Levomäki & Christian Jalio, Forcepoint for
    the report and PoC.

    (backported from commit 8574da1dc1d7250c69eb76213c07c649b6d5a704)

